{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S742zoUYW7CUb1wVTHDSEr","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Claim 1 主证据锚定在 pairwise 层面（Few-NERD r=0.156 p<1e-11 已有，MAVEN\n2\t  复现 r=0.09 p=0.003）， per-type partial r 作为 supporting evidence 方向正确但仅 marginal (p≈0.065)。\n3\t  第二模型方向一致但效应量弱 (pairwise r=0.09)。Claim 1 措辞从 \"independently predicts\" 软化为 \"contributes\n4\t  to prediction beyond count, with strongest evidence at type-pair mechanistic level\"。\n5\t  Claim 2 双通道基本 additive，2x2 interaction 不显著 (p=0.135)；error taxonomy 方向正确但不完全干净 (high-BCS\n6\t  type_substitution 47% vs low-BCS 18%，但 boundary_error 未完全分离)。 Claim 3 限定适用范围：SDGD\n7\t  在 MAVEN (168 types) 增益 +4.0 F1 显著，Few-NERD (66 types) 仅 +2.3。 SDGD-cal 校准可弥补 SCS\n8\t  噪声 (MAVEN +1.7 over zero)。方法学贡献 (frequency confound 发现、 batch→pairwise→per-type\n9\t  分析演进) 作为独立 contribution。仍冲 EMNLP main，Findings 是现实 fallback。\n10\t\n11\t  '\n12\timagined_experiments:\n13\t- name: MAVEN Confusability Study\n14\t  plan_id: exp-004\n15\t  description: '在 MAVEN (168 FrameNet event types) 上复现 Few-NERD 核心发现：count curve +\n16\t    within-count BCS 相关 + pairwise BCS-confusion 分析。跨任务 (NER→ED) 验证 confusability\n17\t    independence。\n18\t\n19\t    '\n20\t  expected_results:\n21\t    count_1_f1: 0.252\n22\t    count_1_precision: 0.17\n23\t    count_1_recall: 0.485\n24\t    count_1_pred_gold_ratio: 2.85\n25\t    count_6_f1: 0.218\n26\t    count_6_recall: 0.29\n27\t    count_14_f1: 0.198\n28\t    count_14_recall: 0.202\n29\t    count_28_f1: 0.21\n30\t    count_28_recall: 0.182\n31\t    count_56_f1: 0.192\n32\t    count_56_recall: 0.146\n33\t    count_84_f1: 0.168\n34\t    count_84_recall: 0.115\n35\t    count_168_f1: 0.135\n36\t    count_168_recall: 0.082\n37\t    pairwise_n_pairs: 14028\n38\t    pairwise_pearson_r: 0.09\n39\t    pairwise_pearson_p: 0.003\n40\t    pairwise_nonzero_spearman_rho: 0.15\n41\t    pairwise_nonzero_spearman_p: 0.025\n42\t    pairwise_count14_r: 0.06\n43\t    pairwise_count14_p: 0.042\n44\t    pairwise_count28_r: 0.1\n45\t    pairwise_count28_p: 0.009\n46\t    batch_f1_bcs_count14_r: 0.12\n47\t    batch_f1_bcs_count14_p: 0.42\n48\t    batch_f1_bcs_count28_r: 0.28\n49\t    batch_f1_bcs_count28_p: 0.14\n50\t    batch_f1_bcs_partial_r: 0.19\n51\t    batch_f1_bcs_partial_p: 0.24\n52\t    confusion_ratio_extreme_count14: 3.2\n53\t    confusion_ratio_extreme_count28: 2.8\n54\t    confusion_ratio_random_count14: 1.5\n55\t    confusion_ratio_random_count28: 1.9\n56\t    per_type_partial_r: 0.14\n57\t    per_type_partial_p: 0.11\n58\t    wrong_type_count_1: 0\n59\t    wrong_type_count_28: 3800\n60\t    wrong_type_count_168: 11500\n61\t    top_pair_1: Giving <-> Sending (BCS=0.784, confusion=89)\n62\t    top_pair_2: Attack <-> Hostile_encounter (BCS=0.761, confusion=72)\n63\t    top_pair_3: Statement <-> Communication (BCS=0.738, confusion=65)\n64\t  result_rationale: 'MAVEN pairwise r=0.09 弱于 Few-NERD 的 0.156，原因：(1) 168 types 使\n65\t    confusion 更分散， 每对 type 的 base confusion rate 更低，稀释了 SCS-confusion 相关；(2) event\n66\t    triggers 通常是 单 token (动词/名词)，surface form 变异小于 entity mention，boundary 信号不足以区分\n67\t    type confusion； (3) FrameNet 事件类型的细粒度语义区分 (如 Giving vs Sending) 在 embedding space\n68\t    中的 SCS 是不完美的 proxy——实际 confusion 受 context 影响更大。但因 n=14028 远大于 Few-NERD 的 1953，\n69\t    即使 r=0.09 也 significant (p=0.003)。Batch-level 相关不显著 (p=0.24) 复现了 Few-NERD 的 frequency\n70\t    confound 问题——在 168 types 上此 confound 更严重因为 type frequency 分布更 skewed (MAVEN 长尾分布，少数高频\n71\t    event type 主导)。Confusion ratio 在 extreme batches 仅 2.8-3.2x (vs Few-NERD 10-28x)，因\n72\t    168 types 中极端 BCS batch 的 confusability contrast 被稀释。 Count curve 显示 recall 从\n73\t    0.485 降至 0.082——比 Few-NERD (0.641→0.304) 更陡峭，因 168 types 远超模型 attention capacity。\n74\t\n75\t    '\n76\t  tables:\n77\t  - name: MAVEN Count Curve (Qwen3-32B, V2 prompt)\n78\t    columns:\n79\t    - count\n80\t    - F1\n81\t    - Precision\n82\t    - Recall\n83\t    - Pred/Gold\n84\t    - WrongType_count\n85\t    rows:\n86\t    - - 1\n87\t      - 0.252\n88\t      - 0.17\n89\t      - 0.485\n90\t      - 2.85\n91\t      - 0\n92\t    - - 6\n93\t      - 0.218\n94\t      - 0.175\n95\t      - 0.29\n96\t      - 1.66\n97\t      - 620\n98\t    - - 14\n99\t      - 0.198\n100\t      - 0.195\n101\t      - 0.202\n102\t      - 1.04\n103\t      - 1850\n104\t    - - 28\n105\t      - 0.21\n106\t      - 0.248\n107\t      - 0.182\n108\t      - 0.73\n109\t      - 3800\n110\t    - - 56\n111\t      - 0.192\n112\t      - 0.28\n113\t      - 0.146\n114\t      - 0.52\n115\t      - 6200\n116\t    - - 84\n117\t      - 0.168\n118\t      - 0.305\n119\t      - 0.115\n120\t      - 0.38\n121\t      - 8400\n122\t    - - 168\n123\t      - 0.135\n124\t      - 0.34\n125\t      - 0.082\n126\t      - 0.24\n127\t      - 11500\n128\t  - name: MAVEN Pairwise BCS-Confusion Analysis\n129\t    columns:\n130\t    - subset\n131\t    - n_pairs\n132\t    - statistic\n133\t    - value\n134\t    - p\n135\t    rows:\n136\t    - - all\n137\t      - 14028\n138\t      - Pearson r\n139\t      - 0.09\n140\t      - 0.003\n141\t    - - all\n142\t      - 14028\n143\t      - Spearman ρ\n144\t      - 0.1\n145\t      - 0.001\n146\t    - - count_14\n147\t      - 12880\n148\t      - Pearson r\n149\t      - 0.06\n150\t      - 0.042\n151\t    - - count_28\n152\t      - 14028\n153\t      - Pearson r\n154\t      - 0.1\n155\t      - 0.009\n156\t    - - nonzero_only\n157\t      - 580\n158\t      - Spearman ρ\n159\t      - 0.15\n160\t      - 0.025\n161\t  - name: MAVEN Extreme Batch Confusion Ratio\n162\t    columns:\n163\t    - count\n164\t    - high_BCS_confusion_rate\n165\t    - low_BCS_confusion_rate\n166\t    - ratio\n167\t    rows:\n168\t    - - 14\n169\t      - 0.028\n170\t      - 0.0088\n171\t      - 3.2\n172\t    - - 28\n173\t      - 0.038\n174\t      - 0.0136\n175\t      - 2.8\n176\t  figures_description:\n177\t  - 'Fig: MAVEN count curve (F1/P/R vs type count). 与 Few-NERD 并列双面板。Recall 线单调下降\n178\t    (0.485→0.082)，precision 单调上升，F1 inverted-U (peak at count_28)。slope 比 Few-NERD\n179\t    更陡。'\n180\t  - 'Fig: MAVEN pairwise BCS vs confusion count scatter plot. 14028 点 (大部分集中在零附近)，nonzero\n181\t    子集标红，回归线 slope 可见但弱。与 Few-NERD 的 scatter 并列对比。'\n182\t  - 'Fig: MAVEN FrameNet hierarchy 子图——高混淆 sibling 对标注 (Giving/Sending, Attack/Hostile_encounter)，BCS\n183\t    值标注在边上。'\n184\t  analysis: 'MAVEN 跨任务复现方向正确但效应量弱化。Pairwise 分析 (r=0.09, p=0.003) 仍 significant， 可作为\n185\t    Claim 1 的 cross-task supporting evidence，但需承认效应量从 NER 的 r=0.156 降至 ED 的 0.09。\n186\t    Per-type partial r 不显著 (p=0.11)，与 Few-NERD 的 marginal result 一致——两个数据集都显示 per-type\n187\t    层面证据弱于 pairwise。论文叙事应强调：pairwise 分析是免疫 frequency confound 的 mechanistic 证据，cross-task\n188\t    复现确认了现象的 task-agnostic 本质，但效应量的差异需 transparent 报告。 MAVEN 特有的 FrameNet 层级结构提供了额外的\n189\t    qualitative 验证——top confused pairs 全部是 同层级 sibling events，与 FrameNet 文献的 14.6-19.8%\n190\t    sibling confusion rate 吻合。 Count curve 的更陡下降 (recall 从 0.485 到 0.082) 为 SDGD 在大\n191\t    schema 上的增益提供了动机。\n192\t\n193\t    '\n194\t- name: DocRED Confusability Study\n195\t  plan_id: exp-005\n196\t  description: '在 DocRED (96 relation types) 上测试 confusability independence。 Document-level\n197\t    RE 的 scaling stress test。\n198\t\n199\t    '\n200\t  expected_results:\n201\t    count_1_f1: 0.095\n202\t    count_1_recall: 0.21\n203\t    count_6_f1: 0.082\n204\t    count_12_f1: 0.075\n205\t    count_24_f1: 0.068\n206\t    count_48_f1: 0.058\n207\t    count_96_f1: 0.042\n208\t    pairwise_n_pairs: 4560\n209\t    pairwise_pearson_r: 0.055\n210\t    pairwise_pearson_p: 0.065\n211\t    pairwise_nonzero_spearman_rho: 0.1\n212\t    pairwise_nonzero_spearman_p: 0.12\n213\t    per_type_partial_r: 0.08\n214\t    per_type_partial_p: 0.32\n215\t  result_rationale: 'DocRED 的 pairwise r 仅 0.055 (p=0.065，marginal)，原因：(1) document-level\n216\t    RE 的核心难度在于 entity pair identification 和 multi-hop reasoning，这些 confound 远大于 type\n217\t    confusability 的效应； (2) relation types 的 confusability 不仅来自语义相似 (如 headquarters_location\n218\t    vs place_of_birth)， 还来自 entity type 重叠——两者难以通过 SCS 单一维度捕获；(3) 96 types 但 document-level\n219\t    评估的 样本量和信号都比 sentence-level NER/ED 更稀疏。训练-free LLM RE 的整体 F1 极低 (0.04-0.10)， 在此性能区间，噪声掩盖了\n220\t    confusability 信号。此结果建议：论文报告 DocRED 作为 \"scaling stress test\" 但承认 RE 任务的额外 confound\n221\t    限制了 confusability 信号的可检测性。可在 appendix 报告， 不作为主 claim 的核心证据。\n222\t\n223\t    '\n224\t  tables:\n225\t  - name: DocRED Count Curve (Qwen3-32B, V2 prompt)\n226\t    columns:\n227\t    - count\n228\t    - F1\n229\t    - Precision\n230\t    - Recall\n231\t    rows:\n232\t    - - 1\n233\t      - 0.095\n234\t      - 0.058\n235\t      - 0.21\n236\t    - - 6\n237\t      - 0.082\n238\t      - 0.055\n239\t      - 0.175\n240\t    - - 12\n241\t      - 0.075\n242\t      - 0.062\n243\t      - 0.095\n244\t    - - 24\n245\t      - 0.068\n246\t      - 0.07\n247\t      - 0.066\n248\t    - - 48\n249\t      - 0.058\n250\t      - 0.078\n251\t      - 0.046\n252\t    - - 96\n253\t      - 0.042\n254\t      - 0.085\n255\t      - 0.028\n256\t  figures_description:\n257\t  - 'Fig (appendix): DocRED count curve。F1 极低 (0.04-0.10)，recall 下降趋势可见但 noisy。标注\n258\t    training-free RE 的固有难度。'\n259\t  analysis: 'DocRED 结果弱于预期，建议降级为 appendix 材料。主要价值：(1) 确认 count-recall 降解在 RE 任务上也存在\n260\t    (Channel 1 task-agnostic)；(2) 暴露了 confusability 分析在 RE 上的局限—— type confusion 被更大的\n261\t    task-specific confound 掩盖。论文不应将 DocRED 列为 Claim 1 的 核心证据，而是作为 \"boundary condition\"\n262\t    讨论：confusability analysis 在 extraction 性能 极低 (<0.10 F1) 时信号被噪声淹没。如时间紧张 (P1 优先级)，可完全省略而不损害核心论点。\n263\t\n264\t    '\n265\t- name: Interaction Effect 2x2\n266\t  plan_id: exp-006\n267\t  description: 'Few-NERD 上 {count_6, count_22} × {low_BCS, high_BCS} 的 2×2 factorial\n268\t    design。 检验 count 和 confusability 的交互效应——additive vs multiplicative。\n269\t\n270\t    '\n271\t  expected_results:\n272\t    count6_lowBCS_f1: 0.338\n273\t    count6_highBCS_f1: 0.28\n274\t    count22_lowBCS_f1: 0.318\n275\t    count22_highBCS_f1: 0.245\n276\t    count6_lowBCS_recall: 0.45\n277\t    count6_highBCS_recall: 0.412\n278\t    count22_lowBCS_recall: 0.295\n279\t    count22_highBCS_recall: 0.248\n280\t    count6_lowBCS_precision: 0.268\n281\t    count6_highBCS_precision: 0.215\n282\t    count22_lowBCS_precision: 0.352\n283\t    count22_highBCS_precision: 0.243\n284\t    count_main_effect_F: 8.2\n285\t    count_main_effect_p: 0.006\n286\t    count_main_effect_eta2: 0.12\n287\t    bcs_main_effect_F: 5.1\n288\t    bcs_main_effect_p: 0.028\n289\t    bcs_main_effect_eta2: 0.08\n290\t    interaction_F: 2.3\n291\t    interaction_p: 0.135\n292\t    interaction_eta2: 0.04\n293\t    additive_prediction_HH: 0.25\n294\t    actual_HH: 0.245\n295\t    super_additive_residual: -0.005\n296\t    count_effect_on_recall: -0.16\n297\t    count_effect_on_precision: 0.052\n298\t    bcs_effect_on_recall: -0.043\n299\t    bcs_effect_on_precision: -0.081\n300\t    n_per_cell: 12\n301\t  result_rationale: 'Count 主效应显著 (F=8.2, p=0.006)：count_6 vs count_22 的 F1 差异 (~2.7\n302\t    points) 主要由 recall 驱动 (0.431→0.272, Δ=-0.160)，确认 Channel 1 (count→recall) 机制。\n303\t    BCS 主效应显著 (F=5.1, p=0.028)：low vs high BCS 的 F1 差异 (~6.5 points) 同时影响 recall 和\n304\t    precision，但 precision 效应更大 (Δ=-0.081)，因为 type confusion 直接导致 precision 下降。 Interaction\n305\t    不显著 (F=2.3, p=0.135)：additive 预测 (0.250) 与实际 (0.245) 仅差 0.5 point， slight super-additivity\n306\t    因统计功效不足 (n=12/cell) 未达显著。机制解释：count 和 BCS 共享 下游 working memory 资源——当 count 已高时，BCS\n307\t    的额外负担略微放大，但两个通道的主要机制 (attention allocation vs type discrimination) 仍大致独立。此结果支持\n308\t    \"approximately orthogonal\" 但须将 \"orthogonal channels\" 措辞软化为 \"largely additive with\n309\t    marginal interaction\"。\n310\t\n311\t    '\n312\t  tables:\n313\t  - name: 2×2 Factorial Cell Means (F1 / Recall / Precision)\n314\t    columns:\n315\t    - ''\n316\t    - Low BCS\n317\t    - High BCS\n318\t    - BCS Effect\n319\t    rows:\n320\t    - - Count=6\n321\t      - 0.338 / 0.450 / 0.268\n322\t      - 0.280 / 0.412 / 0.215\n323\t      - -0.058 / -0.038 / -0.053\n324\t    - - Count=22\n325\t      - 0.318 / 0.295 / 0.352\n326\t      - 0.245 / 0.248 / 0.243\n327\t      - -0.073 / -0.047 / -0.109\n328\t    - - Count Effect\n329\t      - -0.020 / -0.155 / +0.084\n330\t      - -0.035 / -0.164 / +0.028\n331\t      - ''\n332\t  - name: Two-Way ANOVA Results\n333\t    columns:\n334\t    - Source\n335\t    - F\n336\t    - p\n337\t    - η²\n338\t    - Verdict\n339\t    rows:\n340\t    - - Count (main)\n341\t      - 8.2\n342\t      - 0.006\n343\t      - 0.12\n344\t      - Significant\n345\t    - - BCS (main)\n346\t      - 5.1\n347\t      - 0.028\n348\t      - 0.08\n349\t      - Significant\n350\t    - - Count × BCS\n351\t      - 2.3\n352\t      - 0.135\n353\t      - 0.04\n354\t      - Not significant\n355\t  figures_description:\n356\t  - 'Fig: 2×2 interaction plot。X 轴 count (6, 22)，Y 轴 F1，两条线 (low/high BCS)。近似平行但 high\n357\t    count 端 BCS gap 略大 → mild super-additivity 可视化。附 error bars (±1 SE)。'\n358\t  - 'Fig: Recall 和 Precision 分别的 2×2 interaction plot 并列。Recall 图中 count 线间距大 (Channel\n359\t    1 dominant)，Precision 图中 BCS 线间距大 (Channel 2 dominant)。'\n360\t  analysis: '两个 main effects 均显著 (p<0.05)，interaction 不显著 (p=0.135) → 支持 multi-channel\n361\t    model 的 基本 additive 假设。但 η²(interaction)=0.04 虽不显著，方向是 super-additive (实际 HH 比预测\n362\t    差 0.5 点)，须在论文中 transparent 报告。Channel decomposition 清晰：count 主要影响 recall (Δ=-0.160)，BCS\n363\t    主要影响 precision (Δ=-0.081)。但 BCS 也影响 recall (Δ=-0.043)，说明 confusability 不仅导致 type\n364\t    confusion (precision hit) 还导致部分 entity 被完全遗漏 (model 在 confusable types 间犹豫不决时选择不输出)。这为\n365\t    Claim 2 提供细化： 两通道非完全正交，confusability 有 secondary recall 效应。\n366\t\n367\t    '\n368\t- name: Error Taxonomy by BCS Bin\n369\t  plan_id: exp-007\n370\t  description: '系统 FP/FN 分类 (type_substitution / boundary_error / false_negative /\n371\t    hallucination)， 按 BCS bin 分层。Claim 2 的 mechanistic evidence。\n372\t\n373\t    '\n374\t  expected_results:\n375\t    high_bcs_type_substitution_pct: 0.47\n376\t    high_bcs_boundary_error_pct: 0.12\n377\t    high_bcs_false_negative_pct: 0.33\n378\t    high_bcs_hallucination_pct: 0.08\n379\t    low_bcs_type_substitution_pct: 0.18\n380\t    low_bcs_boundary_error_pct: 0.15\n381\t    low_bcs_false_negative_pct: 0.55\n382\t    low_bcs_hallucination_pct: 0.12\n383\t    mid_bcs_type_substitution_pct: 0.3\n384\t    mid_bcs_false_negative_pct: 0.45\n385\t    type_sub_monotonic_increase_with_bcs: true\n386\t    false_neg_monotonic_decrease_with_bcs: true\n387\t    boundary_err_monotonic: false\n388\t    hallucination_monotonic: false\n389\t    type_sub_ratio_high_vs_low: 2.6\n390\t    chi2_type_sub_vs_bcs_bin: 18.4\n391\t    chi2_p: 0.001\n392\t  result_rationale: 'High-BCS batch 中 type_substitution 占 47%：当 batch 内包含语义相近的 types\n393\t    (如 person-athlete vs person-artist)，模型正确识别 entity span 但选错 type——这正是 confusability\n394\t    的直接机械效应。 Low-BCS batch 中 false_negative 占 55%：当 types 不 confusable 时，主要错误模式变为\n395\t    entity 遗漏 (模型在 prompt 中看到多个不相关 types，attention 分散导致某些 types 的 entities 被忽略)。 趋势不完全干净的原因：(1)\n396\t    boundary_error 不随 BCS 单调变化——它受 entity mention 的 surface form 模糊性影响 (如 \"New York\n397\t    City\" vs \"New York\")，与 type confusability 部分独立； (2) hallucination 在各 bin 间波动 (8-12%)，因为\n398\t    hallucination 主要由模型的 parametric knowledge 驱动，与 batch confusability 无关。Chi-square\n399\t    检验确认 type_substitution 比例与 BCS bin 显著 相关 (p=0.001)，但整体 error taxonomy 不是完美的 four-way\n400\t    separation。\n401\t\n402\t    '\n403\t  tables:\n404\t  - name: Error Distribution by BCS Bin\n405\t    columns:\n406\t    - BCS Bin\n407\t    - type_substitution\n408\t    - boundary_error\n409\t    - false_negative\n410\t    - hallucination\n411\t    - n_errors\n412\t    rows:\n413\t    - - '[0, 0.3)'\n414\t      - 18%\n415\t      - 15%\n416\t      - 55%\n417\t      - 12%\n418\t      - 820\n419\t    - - '[0.3, 0.5)'\n420\t      - 30%\n421\t      - 14%\n422\t      - 45%\n423\t      - 11%\n424\t      - 540\n425\t    - - '[0.5, 0.7)'\n426\t      - 42%\n427\t      - 11%\n428\t      - 38%\n429\t      - 9%\n430\t      - 380\n431\t    - - '[0.7, 1.0]'\n432\t      - 52%\n433\t      - 13%\n434\t      - 28%\n435\t      - 7%\n436\t      - 260\n437\t  - name: Monotonicity Summary\n438\t    columns:\n439\t    - Error Type\n440\t    - Trend with BCS↑\n441\t    - Monotonic?\n442\t    - Chi² p\n443\t    rows:\n444\t    - - type_substitution\n445\t      - ↑ (18→52%)\n446\t      - 'Yes'\n447\t      - '0.001'\n448\t    - - boundary_error\n449\t      - ≈flat (11-15%)\n450\t      - 'No'\n451\t      - '0.62'\n452\t    - - false_negative\n453\t      - ↓ (55→28%)\n454\t      - 'Yes'\n455\t      - '0.003'\n456\t    - - hallucination\n457\t      - ↓ slight (12→7%)\n458\t      - No (non-monotonic at mid)\n459\t      - '0.18'\n460\t  figures_description:\n461\t  - 'Fig: Stacked bar chart，X 轴 BCS bin，Y 轴 error 比例。type_substitution (红) 随 BCS 增长明显，false_negative\n462\t    (蓝) 随 BCS 下降。boundary_error 和 hallucination 相对稳定。'\n463\t  - 'Fig: 典型错误案例展示 (qualitative)。High-BCS batch 中 person-athlete 被标为 person-artist\n464\t    的实例；Low-BCS batch 中 entity 完全遗漏的实例。'\n465\t  analysis: 'Error taxonomy 提供了 multi-channel model 最直接的 mechanistic 支持：type_substitution\n466\t    从 18% (low BCS) 上升到 52% (high BCS)，false_negative 从 55% 下降到 28%。这确认了 confusability\n467\t    驱动 type confusion (Channel 2) 而 count/attention dilution 驱动 entity omission (Channel\n468\t    1)。 但趋势的不完全干净 (boundary_error 无 BCS 趋势、hallucination 非单调) 要求在论文中用 \"dominant error\n469\t    modes shift\" 而非 \"exclusive channels\" 的措辞。Chi-square 显著 (p=0.001) 确保 type_substitution-BCS\n470\t    关系有统计支撑。此分析与 exp-002 的 confusion ratio (10-28x) 互补——后者量化了 confusability 对混淆频率的影响，前者量化了\n471\t    confusability 对 error 类型分布的影响。\n472\t\n473\t    '\n474\t- name: Multi-Model Validation (LLaMA-3.3-70B)\n475\t  plan_id: exp-012\n476\t  description: '用 LLaMA-3.3-70B-Instruct 复现 exp-002 protocol on Few-NERD。 验证 confusability\n477\t    independence 非 model-specific artifact。\n478\t\n479\t    '\n480\t  expected_results:\n481\t    model2_full_schema_f1: 0.385\n482\t    model2_full_schema_precision: 0.59\n483\t    model2_full_schema_recall: 0.285\n484\t    model2_count1_f1: 0.295\n485\t    model2_count1_recall: 0.595\n486\t    model2_count6_f1: 0.278\n487\t    model2_count6_recall: 0.43\n488\t    model2_count12_f1: 0.31\n489\t    model2_count12_recall: 0.305\n490\t    model2_count64_f1: 0.385\n491\t    model2_count64_recall: 0.285\n492\t    model2_pairwise_all_r: 0.09\n493\t    model2_pairwise_all_p: 0.012\n494\t    model2_pairwise_count6_r: 0.04\n495\t    model2_pairwise_count6_p: 0.12\n496\t    model2_pairwise_count12_r: 0.11\n497\t    model2_pairwise_count12_p: 0.008\n498\t    model2_pairwise_nonzero_spearman: 0.17\n499\t    model2_pairwise_nonzero_p: 0.032\n500\t    model2_f1_bcs_partial_r: 0.22\n501\t    model2_f1_bcs_partial_p: 0.11\n502\t    model2_f1_bcs_count12_r: 0.38\n503\t    model2_f1_bcs_count12_p: 0.048\n504\t    model2_per_type_partial_r: 0.15\n505\t    model2_per_type_partial_p: 0.082\n506\t    model2_confusion_ratio_extreme_count12: 7.5\n507\t    model2_confusion_ratio_extreme_count6: 15.2\n508\t    model2_top_pair: person-other <-> person-politician (BCS=0.934, confusion=118)\n509\t  result_rationale: 'LLaMA-3.3-70B 的 pairwise r=0.09 弱于 Qwen3-32B 的 0.156，原因：(1) 不同模型家族对\n510\t    type confusability 有不同的 sensitivity——LLaMA 的 instruction following 和 NER 能力与 Qwen\n511\t    不同， 某些 confusable pairs (如 location subtypes) LLaMA 处理更好，其他 (如 person subtypes)\n512\t    更差， 导致总体 BCS-confusion 相关被 partial cancellation 削弱；(2) LLaMA-3.3 在 70B scale 上的\n513\t    in-context learning 能力可能使其对 type description 的 discrimination 更好，降低了 embedding\n514\t    SCS 的预测力 (模型实际 confusion pattern 与 static embedding SCS 的偏差更大)。 count_6 pairwise\n515\t    r 不显著 (p=0.12) 因为 6 types 下 confusion event 很少——每个 batch 只有 C(6,2)=15 个 type pair，大多数\n516\t    confusion count 为 0，统计检验功效不足。count_12 仍显著 (r=0.11, p=0.008)。Top confused pair\n517\t    仍是 person-other ↔ person-politician (确认 confusion 结构 model-agnostic)。整体全 schema\n518\t    F1=0.385 略低于 Qwen3 的 0.414，可能因 70B < 32B (FP8 quantization 使 Qwen3-32B 的有效参数更多)\n519\t    或 model architecture 差异。\n520\t\n521\t    '\n522\t  tables:\n523\t  - name: Cross-Model Pairwise Comparison\n524\t    columns:\n525\t    - Metric\n526\t    - Qwen3-32B\n527\t    - LLaMA-3.3-70B\n528\t    - Direction Consistent?\n529\t    rows:\n530\t    - - Pairwise r (all)\n531\t      - 0.156\n532\t      - 0.09\n533\t      - Yes (positive)\n534\t    - - Pairwise p (all)\n535\t      - '4.6e-12'\n536\t      - 0.012\n537\t      - Both significant\n538\t    - - Pairwise r (count_6)\n539\t      - 0.078\n540\t      - 0.04\n541\t      - Yes but LLaMA n.s.\n542\t    - - Pairwise r (count_12)\n543\t      - 0.147\n544\t      - 0.11\n545\t      - 'Yes'\n546\t    - - Nonzero Spearman ρ\n547\t      - 0.254\n548\t      - 0.17\n549\t      - 'Yes'\n550\t    - - Confusion ratio (extreme, c12)\n551\t      - 9.9x\n552\t      - 7.5x\n553\t      - 'Yes'\n554\t    - - Top confused pair\n555\t      - person-other↔politician\n556\t      - person-other↔politician\n557\t      - Same pair\n558\t  - name: LLaMA-3.3-70B Count Curve\n559\t    columns:\n560\t    - count\n561\t    - F1\n562\t    - Precision\n563\t    - Recall\n564\t    rows:\n565\t    - - 1\n566\t      - 0.295\n567\t      - 0.195\n568\t      - 0.595\n569\t    - - 6\n570\t      - 0.278\n571\t      - 0.208\n572\t      - 0.43\n573\t    - - 12\n574\t      - 0.31\n575\t      - 0.33\n576\t      - 0.305\n577\t    - - 22\n578\t      - 0.275\n579\t      - 0.315\n580\t      - 0.245\n581\t    - - 44\n582\t      - 0.398\n583\t      - 0.465\n584\t      - 0.348\n585\t    - - 64\n586\t      - 0.385\n587\t      - 0.59\n588\t      - 0.285\n589\t  figures_description:\n590\t  - 'Fig: 双模型 pairwise BCS-confusion scatter plot 并列。Qwen3 (左) 回归线 slope 更陡 (r=0.156)，LLaMA\n591\t    (右) slope 更平 (r=0.09) 但方向一致。'\n592\t  - 'Fig: 双模型 count curve 叠加在同一坐标系。两条 recall 线均单调下降，LLaMA 稍低但趋势平行。'\n593\t  analysis: 'Multi-model validation 确认 confusability-confusion 关系非 model-specific：方向一致、top\n594\t    confused pair 相同、confusion ratio 均为正。但效应量差异 (0.156 vs 0.09) 要求论文承认 \"effect size\n595\t    varies across model families\"。count_6 在 LLaMA 上不显著是功效问题 (小样本 + 弱效应)， 不影响 main\n596\t    claim。论文应报告 cross-model comparison table，强调方向一致性而非效应量匹配。 满足 reviewer \">=2 models\"\n597\t    要求，但 reviewer 可能追问为什么效应量减半——准备好解释： 不同模型的 internal representation 与 static embedding\n598\t    SCS 的对齐程度不同。\n599\t\n600\t    '\n601\t- name: SDGD-zero on Few-NERD\n602\t  plan_id: exp-008\n603\t  description: 'Confusability-minimizing batch composition via embedding SCS + graph\n604\t    coloring on Few-NERD (66 types)。 与 single-pass full-schema baseline 对比。\n605\t\n606\t    '\n607\t  expected_results:\n608\t    scs_threshold: 0.5\n609\t    n_edges_above_threshold: 85\n610\t    chromatic_number: 10\n611\t    avg_batch_size: 6.6\n612\t    max_batch_size: 9\n613\t    min_batch_size: 4\n614\t    max_within_batch_scs: 0.42\n615\t    sdgd_zero_f1: 0.437\n616\t    sdgd_zero_precision: 0.405\n617\t    sdgd_zero_recall: 0.474\n618\t    single_pass_f1: 0.414\n619\t    single_pass_precision: 0.648\n620\t    single_pass_recall: 0.304\n621\t    f1_gain_over_single: 2.3\n622\t    n_merge_conflicts: 145\n623\t    merge_conflict_resolution: confidence-based (max logprob)\n624\t    pct_docs_with_conflicts: 0.18\n625\t    sdgd_wrong_type_count: 1280\n626\t    single_pass_wrong_type_count: 2050\n627\t    wrong_type_reduction_pct: 0.375\n628\t    api_calls_per_doc: 10\n629\t    wall_clock_ratio_vs_single: 8.5\n630\t  result_rationale: 'SDGD-zero 在 66-type Few-NERD 上增益有限 (+2.3 F1) 的原因：(1) 66 types\n631\t    的 confusability 负担中等——只有 ~85 个 type pair SCS>0.5 (out of C(66,2)=2145)，graph coloring\n632\t    的优化空间 有限；(2) single-pass baseline 在 V2 prompt 下已达 F1=0.414，under-prediction (pred/gold=0.47)\n633\t    是主要瓶颈——SDGD 通过降低 batch size 提升了 recall (+0.170) 但同时降低了 precision (-0.243)， 因为小\n634\t    batch 促使模型 over-predict；(3) merge step 引入 ~145 个 span conflict (18% docs 受影响)，\n635\t    confidence-based resolution 不完美——部分 conflict 解决错误抵消了 confusability reduction 的收益。\n636\t    Wrong type count 从 2050 降至 1280 (减少 37.5%) 是 SDGD 的直接 mechanistic 效果—— confusable\n637\t    types 被分到不同 batch 后 type confusion 减少。但 F1 gain 仅 2.3 是因为 wrong type reduction\n638\t    只是 overall error 的一部分——false negative 和 boundary error 未被 SDGD 直接解决。 结论：66 types\n639\t    属于 \"中等 schema\"，SDGD 增益 marginal，consistent with median tier 定义。\n640\t\n641\t    '\n642\t  tables:\n643\t  - name: SDGD-zero vs Single-Pass on Few-NERD\n644\t    columns:\n645\t    - Method\n646\t    - Batches\n647\t    - F1\n648\t    - Precision\n649\t    - Recall\n650\t    - WrongType\n651\t    - API Calls\n652\t    rows:\n653\t    - - Single-pass\n654\t      - 1\n655\t      - 0.414\n656\t      - 0.648\n657\t      - 0.304\n658\t      - 2050\n659\t      - 1\n660\t    - - SDGD-zero\n661\t      - 10\n662\t      - 0.437\n663\t      - 0.405\n664\t      - 0.474\n665\t      - 1280\n666\t      - 10\n667\t    - - Δ\n668\t      - ''\n669\t      - '+2.3'\n670\t      - '-24.3'\n671\t      - '+17.0'\n672\t      - -37.5%\n673\t      - '+9'\n674\t  - name: SDGD Batch Composition Summary\n675\t    columns:\n676\t    - Batch\n677\t    - Size\n678\t    - Max Intra-Batch SCS\n679\t    - Example Types\n680\t    rows:\n681\t    - - 1\n682\t      - 7\n683\t      - 0.38\n684\t      - person-athlete, event-protest, product-car, ...\n685\t    - - 2\n686\t      - 6\n687\t      - 0.35\n688\t      - location-city, art-music, organization-company, ...\n689\t    - - 3\n690\t      - 8\n691\t      - 0.42\n692\t      - person-politician, building-library, event-election, ...\n693\t    - - '...'\n694\t      - '...'\n695\t      - '...'\n696\t      - '...'\n697\t    - - 10\n698\t      - 5\n699\t      - 0.28\n700\t      - other-disease, other-currency, other-language, ...\n701\t  figures_description:\n702\t  - 'Fig: SDGD batch composition 可视化——confusability graph (nodes=types, edges=high\n703\t    SCS pairs)，graph coloring 标注不同颜色。显示 person subtypes 被分到不同 batches。'\n704\t  - 'Fig: Single-pass vs SDGD-zero bar chart (F1, P, R 三组 bars)。标注 F1 gain 和 recall\n705\t    提升。'\n706\t  analysis: 'Few-NERD 上 SDGD-zero 的 +2.3 F1 增益在统计上 marginal (需报 confidence interval)。\n707\t    主要价值在于方向验证——wrong type reduction (37.5%) 确认 confusability-aware grouping 的 mechanistic\n708\t    效果。但在 66-type schema 上，SDGD 的 practical significance 有限—— single-pass 已 decent，decomposition\n709\t    的额外 API cost (10x) 可能不值得。 论文应将 Few-NERD 结果定位为 \"proof of concept\"，MAVEN 结果才是 \"practical\n710\t    demonstration\"。 Precision-recall tradeoff (precision 下降 24 points but recall 上升\n711\t    17 points) 需要在论文中 讨论：SDGD 的 batch size reduction 解决了 under-prediction 问题，但引入了\n712\t    over-prediction。 future work 可结合 SDGD + per-type precision calibration。\n713\t\n714\t    '\n715\t- name: SDGD-zero on MAVEN\n716\t  plan_id: exp-009\n717\t  description: 'SDGD-zero on MAVEN (168 event types)。与 single-pass + random batching\n718\t    对比。 Cross-task validation of SDGD framework (NER→ED)。\n719\t\n720\t    '\n721\t  expected_results:\n722\t    scs_threshold: 0.45\n723\t    n_edges_above_threshold: 230\n724\t    chromatic_number: 22\n725\t    avg_batch_size: 7.6\n726\t    max_batch_size: 11\n727\t    min_batch_size: 5\n728\t    max_within_batch_scs: 0.4\n729\t    sdgd_zero_f1: 0.175\n730\t    sdgd_zero_precision: 0.19\n731\t    sdgd_zero_recall: 0.162\n732\t    single_pass_f1: 0.135\n733\t    single_pass_recall: 0.082\n734\t    random_k22_f1: 0.155\n735\t    random_k22_recall: 0.138\n736\t    f1_gain_over_single: 4.0\n737\t    f1_gain_over_random: 2.0\n738\t    sdgd_vs_single_p: 0.002\n739\t    sdgd_vs_random_p: 0.038\n740\t    sdgd_wrong_type_count: 4200\n741\t    single_pass_wrong_type_count: 11500\n742\t    random_wrong_type_count: 6800\n743\t    api_calls_per_doc: 22\n744\t    wall_clock_ratio_vs_single: 18.5\n745\t    wall_clock_ratio_vs_pertype: 0.2\n746\t  result_rationale: 'MAVEN 上 SDGD-zero 增益更大 (+4.0 F1 over single-pass, +2.0 over random)\n747\t    的原因： (1) 168 types 的 single-pass baseline 极差 (F1=0.135)——模型在一个 prompt 中处理 168\n748\t    个 event type definition 时严重过载，recall 仅 0.082；SDGD 将 batch size 降至 ~7.6 types，\n749\t    recall 从 0.082 提升至 0.162 (几乎翻倍)；(2) FrameNet 层级中 sibling types 的 BCS 很高 (119 pairs\n750\t    > 0.5)，random batching 让这些 sibling 有 ~1/22 概率共现——SDGD 将此概率降至零， 减少了 FrameNet-specific\n751\t    type confusion；(3) wrong type 从 11500 降至 4200 (63% reduction)， 远高于 Few-NERD 的\n752\t    37.5%，说明 confusability-aware grouping 在大 schema 上价值递增。 SDGD vs random delta (+2.0\n753\t    F1) 隔离了 confusability-aware grouping 的 contribution—— random 也帮助 (by reducing\n754\t    count per batch) 但 SDGD 额外分离了 confusable types。 p=0.002 (vs single-pass) 和 p=0.038\n755\t    (vs random) 确认显著性。 此结果是论文 Claim 3 的核心证据——在 ≥100 types 的大 schema 上 SDGD 有 practical\n756\t    significance。\n757\t\n758\t    '\n759\t  tables:\n760\t  - name: SDGD-zero Comparison on MAVEN (168 types)\n761\t    columns:\n762\t    - Method\n763\t    - Batches\n764\t    - F1\n765\t    - Precision\n766\t    - Recall\n767\t    - WrongType\n768\t    - p vs SDGD\n769\t    rows:\n770\t    - - Single-pass\n771\t      - 1\n772\t      - 0.135\n773\t      - 0.34\n774\t      - 0.082\n775\t      - 11500\n776\t      - 0.002\n777\t    - - Random (k=22)\n778\t      - 22\n779\t      - 0.155\n780\t      - 0.175\n781\t      - 0.138\n782\t      - 6800\n783\t      - 0.038\n784\t    - - SDGD-zero (k=22)\n785\t      - 22\n786\t      - 0.175\n787\t      - 0.19\n788\t      - 0.162\n789\t      - 4200\n790\t      - —\n791\t  - name: Cross-Task SDGD Gain Summary\n792\t    columns:\n793\t    - Dataset\n794\t    - Types\n795\t    - SDGD-zero F1\n796\t    - Single F1\n797\t    - Δ F1\n798\t    - Δ WrongType%\n799\t    rows:\n800\t    - - Few-NERD\n801\t      - 66\n802\t      - 0.437\n803\t      - 0.414\n804\t      - '+2.3'\n805\t      - -37.5%\n806\t    - - MAVEN\n807\t      - 168\n808\t      - 0.175\n809\t      - 0.135\n810\t      - '+4.0'\n811\t      - -63.5%\n812\t  figures_description:\n813\t  - 'Fig: SDGD method comparison bar chart on MAVEN。三组 bars (single / random / SDGD-zero)，F1\n814\t    + WrongType count 双 Y 轴。WrongType 的下降趋势与 F1 gain 呼应。'\n815\t  - 'Fig: SDGD gain vs schema size scatter。X 轴 n_types (66, 168)，Y 轴 Δ F1。两个点 + 趋势线显示\n816\t    gain 随 schema size 增长。附虚线标注 Claim 3 的适用范围 (≥100 types)。'\n817\t  analysis: 'MAVEN 结果确认 SDGD 在大 schema (168 types) 上有 substantial 增益——F1 gain +4.0\n818\t    显著 (p=0.002)。与 Few-NERD 的 +2.3 对比形成清晰趋势：SDGD 的价值随 schema complexity (type count\n819\t    × confusability density) 递增。Cross-task 成功 (NER → ED) 支持 SDGD 的 task-agnostic 性质。Random\n820\t    ablation (Δ=+2.0) 确认 confusability-aware grouping 的独立 贡献超越 mere batch count reduction。Wrong\n821\t    type 63.5% 减少是 SDGD 的 headline mechanistic result。论文应将此作为 Claim 3 的 primary evidence，Few-NERD\n822\t    作为 secondary。 局限性：absolute F1=0.175 仍很低——SDGD 改善了 relative performance 但 training-free\n823\t    ED 在 168 types 上仍远落后 supervised method。须在论文中 frame 为 \"SDGD narrows the gap but\n824\t    does not close it\" 并指出 remaining error 来自 non-confusability sources (count capacity,\n825\t    event trigger ambiguity)。\n826\t\n827\t    '\n828\t- name: SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\n829\t  plan_id: exp-010\n830\t  description: '用 5-10 calibration examples 构建 empirical confusion matrix，替换 embedding\n831\t    SCS 做 graph coloring。对比 SDGD-zero。\n832\t\n833\t    '\n834\t  expected_results:\n835\t    n_calibration_examples: 8\n836\t    calibration_api_calls: 528\n837\t    empirical_confusion_pairs_discovered: 42\n838\t    overlap_with_scs_top50: 0.62\n839\t    sdgd_cal_f1: 0.449\n840\t    sdgd_cal_precision: 0.415\n841\t    sdgd_cal_recall: 0.488\n842\t    sdgd_zero_f1: 0.437\n843\t    f1_gain_over_zero: 1.2\n844\t    n_batches_changed: 4\n845\t    types_reassigned: 8\n846\t    new_chromatic_number: 11\n847\t    sdgd_cal_vs_zero_p: 0.15\n848\t  result_rationale: 'SDGD-cal 比 SDGD-zero 仅 +1.2 F1 的原因：(1) 8 个 calibration example\n849\t    对 66×66 confusion matrix 的估计很稀疏——C(66,2)=2145 个 pair 中只有 ~42 个被经验观察到 confused，其余是零，\n850\t    matrix 极度 sparse；(2) SCS top-50 confusable pairs 中 62% 与 empirical confusion 重合——\n851\t    embedding proxy 已捕获主要 confusion 结构，calibration 只修正了 38% 的 \"surprise\" pairs； (3)\n852\t    修正的 8 个 type 重新分配只影响了 4 个 batch，global batch structure 变化有限。 Calibration 的主要价值在于发现\n853\t    SCS 低估的 confusable pairs (如 art-film ↔ art-broadcastprogram， SCS=0.38 但 empirical\n854\t    confusion=12) 和 SCS 高估的 pairs (如 organization-religion ↔ organization-political，SCS=0.72\n855\t    但 confusion=0)。p=0.15 不显著——在 66-type schema 上 calibration 的增量太小。此结果建议 SDGD-cal\n856\t    的价值在大 schema 上更大 (where SCS noise affects more pairs)。\n857\t\n858\t    '\n859\t  tables:\n860\t  - name: SDGD-cal vs SDGD-zero on Few-NERD\n861\t    columns:\n862\t    - Method\n863\t    - F1\n864\t    - P\n865\t    - R\n866\t    - Calibration Cost\n867\t    rows:\n868\t    - - SDGD-zero\n869\t      - 0.437\n870\t      - 0.405\n871\t      - 0.474\n872\t      - 0 examples\n873\t    - - SDGD-cal\n874\t      - 0.449\n875\t      - 0.415\n876\t      - 0.488\n877\t      - 8 examples (528 API calls)\n878\t    - - Δ\n879\t      - '+1.2'\n880\t      - '+1.0'\n881\t      - '+1.4'\n882\t      - ''\n883\t  - name: SCS vs Empirical Confusion Discrepancies (Top 5)\n884\t    columns:\n885\t    - Type Pair\n886\t    - SCS\n887\t    - Empirical Confusion\n888\t    - Direction\n889\t    rows:\n890\t    - - art-film ↔ art-broadcastprogram\n891\t      - 0.38\n892\t      - 12\n893\t      - SCS underestimates\n894\t    - - person-director ↔ person-actor\n895\t      - 0.41\n896\t      - 9\n897\t      - SCS underestimates\n898\t    - - organization-religion ↔ organization-political\n899\t      - 0.72\n900\t      - 0\n901\t      - SCS overestimates\n902\t    - - location-park ↔ location-island\n903\t      - 0.65\n904\t      - 1\n905\t      - SCS overestimates\n906\t    - - person-other ↔ person-scholar\n907\t      - 0.88\n908\t      - 45\n909\t      - SCS accurate\n910\t  figures_description:\n911\t  - 'Fig: SCS vs empirical confusion scatter。每个点是一个 type pair，X=SCS，Y=empirical confusion\n912\t    count。标注 SCS 高估/低估的离群点。回归线 slope 可见但 scatter 大。'\n913\t  analysis: 'Few-NERD 上 SDGD-cal 增益不显著 (p=0.15)，但 mechanistic insight 有价值：SCS 与 empirical\n914\t    confusion 的 overlap 为 62% 意味着 embedding proxy 的 precision 约为 0.62——足以用于 zero-shot\n915\t    SDGD 但有改进空间。SCS 的主要失败模式：(1) 低估跨 subtree 的 confusion (如 art-film ↔ art-broadcastprogram\n916\t    在 Few-NERD hierarchy 中不是 direct sibling 但实际 highly confused)；(2) 高估有明确区分特征的 pairs\n917\t    (如 religion ↔ political 虽语义相近但 entity mention 有明确 lexical 区分)。这些 insight 为 exp-015\n918\t    (SCS validation) 提供预期框架。 对论文的贡献：SDGD-cal 作为 \"how much room for improvement exists\n919\t    over zero-shot\" 的 upper bound indicator，即使在 66-type schema 上增量有限。\n920\t\n921\t    '\n922\t- name: SDGD-cal on MAVEN\n923\t  plan_id: exp-011\n924\t  description: 'SDGD-cal on MAVEN (168 event types)。Empirical calibration on 168 types\n925\t    with 5-10 examples。 Full comparison table。\n926\t\n927\t    '\n928\t  expected_results:\n929\t    n_calibration_examples: 8\n930\t    calibration_api_calls: 1344\n931\t    empirical_confusion_pairs_discovered: 128\n932\t    overlap_with_scs_top100: 0.48\n933\t    sdgd_cal_f1: 0.192\n934\t    sdgd_cal_precision: 0.205\n935\t    sdgd_cal_recall: 0.18\n936\t    sdgd_zero_f1: 0.175\n937\t    f1_gain_over_zero: 1.7\n938\t    sdgd_cal_vs_zero_p: 0.045\n939\t    types_reassigned: 24\n940\t    new_chromatic_number: 24\n941\t    sdgd_cal_wrong_type: 3500\n942\t    sdgd_zero_wrong_type: 4200\n943\t    wrong_type_reduction_vs_zero: 0.167\n944\t  result_rationale: 'SDGD-cal 在 MAVEN 上增益更大 (+1.7 F1, p=0.045 marginal significant)，原因：\n945\t    (1) 168 types 使 SCS 的累积误差更大——SCS top-100 confusable pairs 中只有 48% 与 empirical\n946\t    confusion 重合 (vs Few-NERD 的 62%)，因为 FrameNet 事件类型的细粒度语义区分在 embedding space 中表示不够准确\n947\t    (如 Giving vs Commerce_sell, SCS=0.35 但 empirical confusion 高)； (2) calibration\n948\t    发现了 24 个需要重新分配的 types (vs Few-NERD 的 8)，batch 结构变化更大； (3) wrong type 进一步减少 16.7%\n949\t    (4200→3500) 确认 calibration 修正了 SCS 的 false negatives。 Marginal significance (p=0.045)\n950\t    勉强过线，robustness 需额外 validation——如换 random seed 重复 calibration sampling，p 值可能波动到\n951\t    0.05 以上。此结果支持 \"calibration 对大 schema 有价值\"，但收益的 cost-effectiveness (1344 额外 API\n952\t    调用换 +1.7 F1) 需在论文中讨论。\n953\t\n954\t    '\n955\t  tables:\n956\t  - name: Full Comparison Table — MAVEN\n957\t    columns:\n958\t    - Method\n959\t    - k\n960\t    - F1\n961\t    - P\n962\t    - R\n963\t    - WrongType\n964\t    - Total API Calls\n965\t    - p vs best\n966\t    rows:\n967\t    - - Single-pass\n968\t      - 1\n969\t      - 0.135\n970\t      - 0.34\n971\t      - 0.082\n972\t      - 11500\n973\t      - 710\n974\t      - <0.001\n975\t    - - Random (k=22)\n976\t      - 22\n977\t      - 0.155\n978\t      - 0.175\n979\t      - 0.138\n980\t      - 6800\n981\t      - 15620\n982\t      - 0.005\n983\t    - - SDGD-zero\n984\t      - 22\n985\t      - 0.175\n986\t      - 0.19\n987\t      - 0.162\n988\t      - 4200\n989\t      - 15620\n990\t      - 0.045\n991\t    - - SDGD-cal\n992\t      - 24\n993\t      - 0.192\n994\t      - 0.205\n995\t      - 0.18\n996\t      - 3500\n997\t      - 15620+1344\n998\t      - —\n999\t    - - Per-type\n1000\t      - 168\n1001\t      - 0.195\n1002\t      - 0.15\n1003\t      - 0.28\n1004\t      - 1800\n1005\t      - 119280\n1006\t      - 0.82\n1007\t  - name: Full Comparison Table — Few-NERD\n1008\t    columns:\n1009\t    - Method\n1010\t    - k\n1011\t    - F1\n1012\t    - P\n1013\t    - R\n1014\t    - WrongType\n1015\t    - Total API Calls\n1016\t    - p vs best\n1017\t    rows:\n1018\t    - - Single-pass\n1019\t      - 1\n1020\t      - 0.414\n1021\t      - 0.648\n1022\t      - 0.304\n1023\t      - 2050\n1024\t      - 500\n1025\t      - 0.003\n1026\t    - - Random (k=10)\n1027\t      - 10\n1028\t      - 0.423\n1029\t      - 0.395\n1030\t      - 0.455\n1031\t      - 1650\n1032\t      - 5000\n1033\t      - 0.08\n1034\t    - - SDGD-zero\n1035\t      - 10\n1036\t      - 0.437\n1037\t      - 0.405\n1038\t      - 0.474\n1039\t      - 1280\n1040\t      - 5000\n1041\t      - 0.15\n1042\t    - - SDGD-cal\n1043\t      - 11\n1044\t      - 0.449\n1045\t      - 0.415\n1046\t      - 0.488\n1047\t      - 1100\n1048\t      - 5000+528\n1049\t      - —\n1050\t    - - Per-type\n1051\t      - 66\n1052\t      - 0.47\n1053\t      - 0.385\n1054\t      - 0.602\n1055\t      - 650\n1056\t      - 33000\n1057\t      - 0.18\n1058\t  figures_description:\n1059\t  - 'Fig: Full method comparison on MAVEN (grouped bar chart)。五种方法的 F1, P, R 三组 bars。标注\n1060\t    statistical significance brackets。'\n1061\t  - 'Fig: SDGD-cal vs SDGD-zero 的 batch reassignment 可视化 (MAVEN)。Sankey diagram 显示\n1062\t    calibration 后 24 个 types 从原 batch 迁移到新 batch。标注迁移原因 (SCS underestimate/overestimate)。'\n1063\t  - 'Fig: Cost-effectiveness plot。X=total API calls，Y=F1。五种方法标点，连 Pareto frontier。SDGD-zero\n1064\t    和 SDGD-cal 在 frontier 上，per-type 不在 (cost 太高 for marginal gain)。'\n1065\t  analysis: 'MAVEN 上 SDGD-cal 是最佳方法 (F1=0.192)，但与 per-type splitting (F1=0.195) 几乎持平\n1066\t    (p=0.82 no significant difference)——这出乎意料地好，因为 SDGD-cal 只用 24 batches vs per-type\n1067\t    的 168。Cost-effectiveness 是 SDGD 的核心卖点：相近质量，~15% latency。 Cross-dataset 对比揭示 SDGD\n1068\t    的适用范围：(1) ≥100 types: SDGD-zero already significant, SDGD-cal further improves;\n1069\t    (2) 30-66 types: gains marginal, calibration not cost-effective; (3) <30 types:\n1070\t    SDGD unnecessary (single-pass sufficient)。这为论文的 Claim 3 限定了清晰的 适用条件。Full comparison\n1071\t    table (两个 dataset × 五种方法) 是论文 Table 1 的核心。\n1072\t\n1073\t    '\n1074\t- name: Random Batching Ablation\n1075\t  plan_id: exp-013\n1076\t  description: 'Same batch count k as SDGD, random composition。隔离 confusability-aware\n1077\t    grouping 的增量贡献。\n1078\t\n1079\t    '\n1080\t  expected_results:\n1081\t    random_k10_fewnerd_f1: 0.423\n1082\t    random_k10_fewnerd_precision: 0.395\n1083\t    random_k10_fewnerd_recall: 0.455\n1084\t    sdgd_zero_fewnerd_f1: 0.437\n1085\t    delta_fewnerd: 1.4\n1086\t    delta_fewnerd_p: 0.08\n1087\t    random_k22_maven_f1: 0.155\n1088\t    sdgd_zero_maven_f1: 0.175\n1089\t    delta_maven: 2.0\n1090\t    delta_maven_p: 0.018\n1091\t    random_mean_within_batch_bcs_fewnerd: 0.285\n1092\t    sdgd_mean_within_batch_bcs_fewnerd: 0.168\n1093\t    random_mean_within_batch_bcs_maven: 0.235\n1094\t    sdgd_mean_within_batch_bcs_maven: 0.145\n1095\t    random_f1_std_fewnerd: 0.008\n1096\t    random_f1_std_maven: 0.006\n1097\t    n_random_seeds: 5\n1098\t  result_rationale: 'Random batching vs single-pass 的增益 (Few-NERD +0.9, MAVEN +2.0)\n1099\t    来自纯粹的 batch size reduction (Channel 1 mitigation)——fewer types per batch → higher\n1100\t    recall。SDGD 的额外增益 (Few-NERD +1.4, MAVEN +2.0) 来自 confusability-aware grouping\n1101\t    (Channel 2 mitigation)—— within-batch BCS 从 random 的 0.285 降至 SDGD 的 0.168，减少了\n1102\t    type confusion。 Few-NERD 上 delta=1.4 仅 marginal significant (p=0.08) 因为 66 types\n1103\t    中 high-BCS pairs 少， random batching 已有 ~90% 概率将 confusable pairs 分开 (with 10 batches,\n1104\t    co-occurrence probability = 1/10 = 10%)。MAVEN 上 delta=2.0 significant (p=0.018)\n1105\t    因为 168 types 中 high-BCS pairs 更多 (119 pairs > 0.5)，random batching 只有 ~95.5% 概率分开\n1106\t    (with 22 batches, co-occurrence = 1/22 = 4.5%)——但 4.5% of 119 pairs ≈ 5.4 confusable\n1107\t    pairs 平均 仍同 batch，SDGD 将此降至零。Random F1 的跨 seed variance 很小 (σ=0.006-0.008)，确认\n1108\t    ablation 结果 robust。\n1109\t\n1110\t    '\n1111\t  tables:\n1112\t  - name: Random vs SDGD Ablation\n1113\t    columns:\n1114\t    - Dataset\n1115\t    - Single-pass F1\n1116\t    - Random F1 (mean±σ)\n1117\t    - SDGD-zero F1\n1118\t    - Δ Random\n1119\t    - Δ SDGD-Random\n1120\t    - p (SDGD vs Rand)\n1121\t    rows:\n1122\t    - - Few-NERD (66)\n1123\t      - 0.414\n1124\t      - 0.423±0.008\n1125\t      - 0.437\n1126\t      - '+0.9'\n1127\t      - '+1.4'\n1128\t      - 0.08\n1129\t    - - MAVEN (168)\n1130\t      - 0.135\n1131\t      - 0.155±0.006\n1132\t      - 0.175\n1133\t      - '+2.0'\n1134\t      - '+2.0'\n1135\t      - 0.018\n1136\t  - name: Within-Batch BCS Analysis\n1137\t    columns:\n1138\t    - Method\n1139\t    - Mean Within-Batch BCS (Few-NERD)\n1140\t    - Mean Within-Batch BCS (MAVEN)\n1141\t    rows:\n1142\t    - - Random\n1143\t      - 0.285\n1144\t      - 0.235\n1145\t    - - SDGD-zero\n1146\t      - 0.168\n1147\t      - 0.145\n1148\t    - - Reduction\n1149\t      - -41%\n1150\t      - -38%\n1151\t  figures_description:\n1152\t  - 'Fig: Ablation bar chart。三组 bars (single / random / SDGD) on each dataset。标注 decomposition\n1153\t    (random - single = Channel 1 gain) and (SDGD - random = Channel 2 gain)。'\n1154\t  - 'Fig: 5 random seeds 的 F1 分布 (violin plot or dot plot) vs SDGD 的单点。可视化 SDGD consistently\n1155\t    above random。'\n1156\t  analysis: 'Ablation 成功隔离了两个 contribution：batch size reduction (Channel 1) 和 confusability-aware\n1157\t    grouping (Channel 2)。在 MAVEN 上两者贡献相当 (各 +2.0 F1)；在 Few-NERD 上 Channel 1 贡献较小 (+0.9)\n1158\t    因为 66 types 的 single-pass recall (0.304) 虽不高但不 catastrophic。 SDGD vs random delta\n1159\t    在 Few-NERD 上 marginal (p=0.08) 是可预期的——这正是 median tier 的 核心特征：SDGD 在中等 schema 上增益\n1160\t    marginal。论文应 frame 为：\"The confusability-aware contribution scales with schema\n1161\t    size: moderate on 66 types, significant on 168 types.\"\n1162\t\n1163\t    '\n1164\t- name: Per-Type Splitting Ablation\n1165\t  plan_id: exp-014\n1166\t  description: 'Per-type splitting (1 type per batch, UniNER-style)。质量上限 + latency\n1167\t    vs quality tradeoff。\n1168\t\n1169\t    '\n1170\t  expected_results:\n1171\t    pertype_fewnerd_f1: 0.47\n1172\t    pertype_fewnerd_precision: 0.385\n1173\t    pertype_fewnerd_recall: 0.602\n1174\t    pertype_fewnerd_api_calls: 33000\n1175\t    pertype_fewnerd_wrong_type: 650\n1176\t    pertype_maven_f1: 0.195\n1177\t    pertype_maven_precision: 0.15\n1178\t    pertype_maven_recall: 0.28\n1179\t    pertype_maven_api_calls: 119280\n1180\t    pertype_maven_wrong_type: 1800\n1181\t    sdgd_vs_pertype_f1_ratio_fewnerd: 0.93\n1182\t    sdgd_vs_pertype_f1_ratio_maven: 0.897\n1183\t    sdgd_vs_pertype_latency_ratio_fewnerd: 0.18\n1184\t    sdgd_vs_pertype_latency_ratio_maven: 0.2\n1185\t    pertype_merge_conflicts_fewnerd: 850\n1186\t    pertype_pct_docs_with_conflicts_fewnerd: 0.72\n1187\t    pertype_merge_conflicts_maven: 2400\n1188\t    pertype_pct_docs_with_conflicts_maven: 0.85\n1189\t  result_rationale: 'Per-type splitting achieves highest recall (Few-NERD 0.602, MAVEN\n1190\t    0.280) because each entity type gets the model''s full attention — no competition\n1191\t    from other types. 但 precision 较低 (Few-NERD 0.385, MAVEN 0.150) 因为 count_1 的 over-prediction\n1192\t    问题 (pred/gold ~2.85-2.97)：当只给模型一个 type 时， 它倾向于将更多 spans 标为该 type。Merge step 产生大量\n1193\t    conflict (72-85% docs 受影响)——当同一 span 被多个 single-type passes 标注时，confidence-based\n1194\t    resolution 不完美。 SDGD/per-type F1 ratio 为 0.93 (Few-NERD) 和 0.90 (MAVEN)：SDGD 在\n1195\t    ~18-20% latency 下 达到 per-type 90-93% 的 F1——这是 cost-effective 的 \"sweet spot\"。Per-type\n1196\t    的 wrong type 更少 (650 vs SDGD 1280 on Few-NERD) 因为 type confusion 在单 type batch\n1197\t    中不可能发生——所有 wrong type 来自 merge conflict resolution 错误。MAVEN 上 per-type F1=0.195\n1198\t    与 SDGD-cal 的 0.192 几乎相同 (p=0.82)，但 API cost 是 7.5x (119280 vs 15620+1344)—— 这是\n1199\t    SDGD 最强的 practical argument。\n1200\t\n1201\t    '\n1202\t  tables:\n1203\t  - name: Per-Type vs SDGD Tradeoff\n1204\t    columns:\n1205\t    - ''\n1206\t    - Few-NERD (66 types)\n1207\t    - MAVEN (168 types)\n1208\t    rows:\n1209\t    - - Per-type F1\n1210\t      - 0.47\n1211\t      - 0.195\n1212\t    - - SDGD-zero F1\n1213\t      - 0.437\n1214\t      - 0.175\n1215\t    - - SDGD-cal F1\n1216\t      - 0.449\n1217\t      - 0.192\n1218\t    - - SDGD-zero/Per-type F1\n1219\t      - 93.0%\n1220\t      - 89.7%\n1221\t    - - SDGD-cal/Per-type F1\n1222\t      - 95.5%\n1223\t      - 98.5%\n1224\t    - - SDGD Latency/Per-type Latency\n1225\t      - 18%\n1226\t      - 20%\n1227\t    - - Per-type Merge Conflicts\n1228\t      - 850 (72% docs)\n1229\t      - 2400 (85% docs)\n1230\t  figures_description:\n1231\t  - 'Fig: Cost-effectiveness Pareto frontier。X=API calls (log scale)，Y=F1。标注 five\n1232\t    methods on both datasets。SDGD 在 Pareto frontier 上，per-type 在 frontier 外 (dominated\n1233\t    on MAVEN by SDGD-cal)。'\n1234\t  - 'Fig: Merge conflict analysis。Per-type 的 conflict 类型分布：correct resolution, type\n1235\t    error introduced by merge, span boundary error from merge。显示 merge 是 per-type\n1236\t    的主要 bottleneck。'\n1237\t  analysis: 'Per-type splitting 是 quality upper bound 但 cost prohibitive——在 MAVEN\n1238\t    上 119K API calls 换来的 F1 (0.195) 与 SDGD-cal 的 17K calls (0.192) 几乎相同。这个结果是论文最有力的\n1239\t    practical argument：\"SDGD achieves 93-99% of the decomposition upper bound at 18-20%\n1240\t    of the cost.\" Merge conflicts 是 per-type 的 Achilles heel——72-85% docs 有 conflict，resolution\n1241\t    引入新错误。 SDGD 的 batch 设计自然减少了 conflict (fewer batches = fewer merge opportunities\n1242\t    + each batch has non-confusable types so span overlap is less ambiguous)。论文应 frame\n1243\t    per-type as \"naive decomposition\" 的 upper bound，SDGD as \"principled decomposition\"\n1244\t    的 practical optimum。\n1245\t\n1246\t    '\n1247\t- name: SCS Validation (Embedding vs Empirical)\n1248\t  plan_id: exp-015\n1249\t  description: 'Spearman/Kendall rank correlation between embedding-based SCS and\n1250\t    empirical confusion matrix from calibration (exp-010)。验证 embedding proxy 的实际 utility。\n1251\t\n1252\t    '\n1253\t  expected_results:\n1254\t    spearman_rho: 0.38\n1255\t    spearman_p: 1.0e-05\n1256\t    kendall_tau: 0.27\n1257\t    kendall_p: 3.0e-05\n1258\t    top50_pairs_precision: 0.62\n1259\t    top50_pairs_recall: 0.45\n1260\t    top100_pairs_precision: 0.48\n1261\t    top100_pairs_recall: 0.52\n1262\t    n_scs_overestimate: 35\n1263\t    n_scs_underestimate: 28\n1264\t    mean_scs_of_overestimates: 0.68\n1265\t    mean_scs_of_underestimates: 0.32\n1266\t    fewnerd_spearman: 0.42\n1267\t    maven_spearman: 0.34\n1268\t  result_rationale: 'Spearman ρ=0.38 的 moderate correlation 反映了 embedding SCS 作为 confusability\n1269\t    proxy 的 固有局限：(1) SCS 基于 type name/description 的 static embedding，而实际 confusion\n1270\t    受 entity mention surface form、context distribution、model-specific representation\n1271\t    共同影响—— static embedding 只能捕获其中的 semantic relatedness component；(2) 高 SCS 不必然导致\n1272\t    high confusion——有些语义相近的 types 有明确的 lexical/morphological cue 帮助区分 (如 organization-religion\n1273\t    vs organization-political，organizations named \"Church of X\" vs \"X Party\" 容易区分)；(3)\n1274\t    低 SCS pair 可能因 dataset-specific 原因 highly confused (如 art-film ↔ art-broadcastprogram，在\n1275\t    Few-NERD 中 film/TV 的 entity mention 经常相同)。 Few-NERD ρ=0.42 高于 MAVEN ρ=0.34 因为\n1276\t    NER 的 entity type 更直接反映在 entity mention 的 surface form 中 (proper nouns 有 type\n1277\t    signal)，而 event triggers 更 ambiguous (同一动词 可能是不同 event type)。Top-50 precision=0.62\n1278\t    意味着 SCS 推荐的 top-50 confusable pairs 中 62% 确实是 empirically confused——足以让 SDGD-zero\n1279\t    outperform random，但留有 calibration 改进空间。\n1280\t\n1281\t    '\n1282\t  tables:\n1283\t  - name: SCS Validation Summary\n1284\t    columns:\n1285\t    - Metric\n1286\t    - Few-NERD\n1287\t    - MAVEN\n1288\t    - Overall\n1289\t    rows:\n1290\t    - - Spearman ρ\n1291\t      - 0.42\n1292\t      - 0.34\n1293\t      - 0.38\n1294\t    - - Kendall τ\n1295\t      - 0.3\n1296\t      - 0.24\n1297\t      - 0.27\n1298\t    - - Top-50 Precision\n1299\t      - 0.68\n1300\t      - 0.56\n1301\t      - 0.62\n1302\t    - - Top-50 Recall\n1303\t      - 0.5\n1304\t      - 0.4\n1305\t      - 0.45\n1306\t    - - n overestimates (SCS high, confusion low)\n1307\t      - 15\n1308\t      - 20\n1309\t      - 35\n1310\t    - - n underestimates (SCS low, confusion high)\n1311\t      - 10\n1312\t      - 18\n1313\t      - 28\n1314\t  - name: SCS Failure Mode Examples\n1315\t    columns:\n1316\t    - Type Pair\n1317\t    - SCS\n1318\t    - Empirical Confusion\n1319\t    - Failure Type\n1320\t    - Explanation\n1321\t    rows:\n1322\t    - - org-religion ↔ org-political\n1323\t      - 0.72\n1324\t      - 0\n1325\t      - Overestimate\n1326\t      - Distinctive entity lexical cues\n1327\t    - - location-park ↔ location-island\n1328\t      - 0.65\n1329\t      - 1\n1330\t      - Overestimate\n1331\t      - Rare co-occurrence in data\n1332\t    - - art-film ↔ art-broadcastprogram\n1333\t      - 0.38\n1334\t      - 12\n1335\t      - Underestimate\n1336\t      - Shared entity mentions (titles)\n1337\t    - - Giving ↔ Commerce_sell\n1338\t      - 0.35\n1339\t      - 8\n1340\t      - Underestimate\n1341\t      - Frame semantics not in embeddings\n1342\t  figures_description:\n1343\t  - 'Fig: SCS vs empirical confusion scatter (log scale Y)。每点一个 type pair。回归线 + confidence\n1344\t    band。标注 overestimate zone (top-left) 和 underestimate zone (bottom-right)。Few-NERD\n1345\t    蓝点，MAVEN 红点。'\n1346\t  - 'Fig: Precision-recall curve for SCS as confusion predictor。X=recall，Y=precision，SCS\n1347\t    threshold 从高到低扫描。标注 optimal threshold point。'\n1348\t  analysis: SCS validation 为 SDGD 框架的 theoretical grounding 提供了关键证据：ρ=0.38 说明 embedding\n1349\t    SCS 是 \"useful but imperfect\" proxy。这解释了 (1) 为什么 SDGD-zero 优于 random (SCS 捕获了 主要\n1350\t    confusion 结构)，(2) 为什么 SDGD-cal 优于 SDGD-zero (calibration 修正了 SCS 的 38% false positive\n1351\t    + 55% false negative)，(3) 为什么 MAVEN 上 SCS 更不准确 (ρ=0.34 vs 0.42) 导致 SDGD-cal 在\n1352\t    MAVEN 上增益更大 (+1.7 vs +1.2)。 论文应将 SCS validation 放在 method section 作为 SDGD 的 justification：\n1353\t    \"We validate that embedding-based SCS provides a moderate but actionable signal\n1354\t    for type confusability (ρ=0.38), sufficient for zero-shot decomposition but improvable\n1355\t    with calibration.\" 此结果也回应 reviewer 对 \"confusability measure validity\" 的 concern——SCS\n1356\t    不完美但 empirically validated，且 imperfection 有清晰的 failure mode taxonomy。\n1357\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5eba5149-decb-42fd-9375-14d22c483592","uuid":"caa46b37-7ced-4883-b96d-7d6df826c88f","timestamp":"2026-05-15T06:18:53.150Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_18/projects/schema-dag-extraction/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T053106/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Claim 1 主证据锚定在 pairwise 层面（Few-NERD r=0.156 p<1e-11 已有，MAVEN\n  复现 r=0.09 p=0.003）， per-type partial r 作为 supporting evidence 方向正确但仅 marginal (p≈0.065)。\n  第二模型方向一致但效应量弱 (pairwise r=0.09)。Claim 1 措辞从 \"independently predicts\" 软化为 \"contributes\n  to prediction beyond count, with strongest evidence at type-pair mechanistic level\"。\n  Claim 2 双通道基本 additive，2x2 interaction 不显著 (p=0.135)；error taxonomy 方向正确但不完全干净 (high-BCS\n  type_substitution 47% vs low-BCS 18%，但 boundary_error 未完全分离)。 Claim 3 限定适用范围：SDGD\n  在 MAVEN (168 types) 增益 +4.0 F1 显著，Few-NERD (66 types) 仅 +2.3。 SDGD-cal 校准可弥补 SCS\n  噪声 (MAVEN +1.7 over zero)。方法学贡献 (frequency confound 发现、 batch→pairwise→per-type\n  分析演进) 作为独立 contribution。仍冲 EMNLP main，Findings 是现实 fallback。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: MAVEN Confusability Study\n  plan_id: exp-004\n  description: '在 MAVEN (168 FrameNet event types) 上复现 Few-NERD 核心发现：count curve +\n    within-count BCS 相关 + pairwise BCS-confusion 分析。跨任务 (NER→ED) 验证 confusability\n    independence。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    count_1_f1: 0.252\n    count_1_precision: 0.17\n    count_1_recall: 0.485\n    count_1_pred_gold_ratio: 2.85\n    count_6_f1: 0.218\n    count_6_recall: 0.29\n    count_14_f1: 0.198\n    count_14_recall: 0.202\n    count_28_f1: 0.21\n    count_28_recall: 0.182\n    count_56_f1: 0.192\n    count_56_recall: 0.146\n    count_84_f1: 0.168\n    count_84_recall: 0.115\n    count_168_f1: 0.135\n    count_168_recall: 0.082\n    pairwise_n_pairs: 14028\n    pairwise_pearson_r: 0.09\n    pairwise_pearson_p: 0.003\n    pairwise_nonzero_spearman_rho: 0.15\n    pairwise_nonzero_spearman_p: 0.025\n    pairwise_count14_r: 0.06\n    pairwise_count14_p: 0.042\n    pairwise_count28_r: 0.1\n    pairwise_count28_p: 0.009\n    batch_f1_bcs_count14_r: 0.12\n    batch_f1_bcs_count14_p: 0.42\n    batch_f1_bcs_count28_r: 0.28\n    batch_f1_bcs_count28_p: 0.14\n    batch_f1_bcs_partial_r: 0.19\n    batch_f1_bcs_partial_p: 0.24\n    confusion_ratio_extreme_count14: 3.2\n    confusion_ratio_extreme_count28: 2.8\n    confusion_ratio_random_count14: 1.5\n    confusion_ratio_random_count28: 1.9\n    per_type_partial_r: 0.14\n    per_type_partial_p: 0.11\n    wrong_type_count_1: 0\n    wrong_type_count_28: 3800\n    wrong_type_count_168: 11500\n    top_pair_1: Giving <-> Sending (BCS=0.784, confusion=89)\n    top_pair_2: Attack <-> Hostile_encounter (BCS=0.761, confusion=72)\n    top_pair_3: Statement <-> Communication (BCS=0.738, confusion=65)\n  result_rationale: 'MAVEN pairwise r=0.09 弱于 Few-NERD 的 0.156，原因：(1) 168 types 使\n    confusion 更分散， 每对 type 的 base confusion rate 更低，稀释了 SCS-confusion 相关；(2) event\n    triggers 通常是 单 token (动词/名词)，surface form 变异小于 entity mention，boundary 信号不足以区分\n    type confusion； (3) FrameNet 事件类型的细粒度语义区分 (如 Giving vs Sending) 在 embedding space\n    中的 SCS 是不完美的 proxy——实际 confusion 受 context 影响更大。但因 n=14028 远大于 Few-NERD 的 1953，\n    即使 r=0.09 也 significant (p=0.003)。Batch-level 相关不显著 (p=0.24) 复现了 Few-NERD 的 frequency\n    confound 问题——在 168 types 上此 confound 更严重因为 type frequency 分布更 skewed (MAVEN 长尾分布，少数高频\n    event type 主导)。Confusion ratio 在 extreme batches 仅 2.8-3.2x (vs Few-NERD 10-28x)，因\n    168 types 中极端 BCS batch 的 confusability contrast 被稀释。 Count curve 显示 recall 从\n    0.485 降至 0.082——比 Few-NERD (0.641→0.304) 更陡峭，因 168 types 远超模型 attention capacity。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: MAVEN Count Curve (Qwen3-32B, V2 prompt)\n    columns:\n    - count\n    - F1\n    - Precision\n    - Recall\n    - Pred/Gold\n    - WrongType_count\n    rows:\n    - - 1\n      - 0.252\n      - 0.17\n      - 0.485\n      - 2.85\n      - 0\n    - - 6\n      - 0.218\n      - 0.175\n      - 0.29\n      - 1.66\n      - 620\n    - - 14\n      - 0.198\n      - 0.195\n      - 0.202\n      - 1.04\n      - 1850\n    - - 28\n      - 0.21\n      - 0.248\n      - 0.182\n      - 0.73\n      - 3800\n    - - 56\n      - 0.192\n      - 0.28\n      - 0.146\n      - 0.52\n      - 6200\n    - - 84\n      - 0.168\n      - 0.305\n      - 0.115\n      - 0.38\n      - 8400\n    - - 168\n      - 0.135\n      - 0.34\n      - 0.082\n      - 0.24\n      - 11500\n  - name: MAVEN Pairwise BCS-Confusion Analysis\n    columns:\n    - subset\n    - n_pairs\n    - statistic\n    - value\n    - p\n    rows:\n    - - all\n      - 14028\n      - Pearson r\n      - 0.09\n      - 0.003\n    - - all\n      - 14028\n      - Spearman ρ\n      - 0.1\n      - 0.001\n    - - count_14\n      - 12880\n      - Pearson r\n      - 0.06\n      - 0.042\n    - - count_28\n      - 14028\n      - Pearson r\n      - 0.1\n      - 0.009\n    - - nonzero_only\n      - 580\n      - Spearman ρ\n      - 0.15\n      - 0.025\n  - name: MAVEN Extreme Batch Confusion Ratio\n    columns:\n    - count\n    - high_BCS_confusion_rate\n    - low_BCS_confusion_rate\n    - ratio\n    rows:\n    - - 14\n      - 0.028\n      - 0.0088\n      - 3.2\n    - - 28\n      - 0.038\n      - 0.0136\n      - 2.8\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: MAVEN count curve (F1/P/R vs type count). 与 Few-NERD 并列双面板。Recall 线单调下降\n    (0.485→0.082)，precision 单调上升，F1 inverted-U (peak at count_28)。slope 比 Few-NERD\n    更陡。'\n  - 'Fig: MAVEN pairwise BCS vs confusion count scatter plot. 14028 点 (大部分集中在零附近)，nonzero\n    子集标红，回归线 slope 可见但弱。与 Few-NERD 的 scatter 并列对比。'\n  - 'Fig: MAVEN FrameNet hierarchy 子图——高混淆 sibling 对标注 (Giving/Sending, Attack/Hostile_encounter)，BCS\n    值标注在边上。'\n  analysis: 'MAVEN 跨任务复现方向正确但效应量弱化。Pairwise 分析 (r=0.09, p=0.003) 仍 significant， 可作为\n    Claim 1 的 cross-task supporting evidence，但需承认效应量从 NER 的 r=0.156 降至 ED 的 0.09。\n    Per-type partial r 不显著 (p=0.11)，与 Few-NERD 的 marginal result 一致——两个数据集都显示 per-type\n    层面证据弱于 pairwise。论文叙事应强调：pairwise 分析是免疫 frequency confound 的 mechanistic 证据，cross-task\n    复现确认了现象的 task-agnostic 本质，但效应量的差异需 transparent 报告。 MAVEN 特有的 FrameNet 层级结构提供了额外的\n    qualitative 验证——top confused pairs 全部是 同层级 sibling events，与 FrameNet 文献的 14.6-19.8%\n    sibling confusion rate 吻合。 Count curve 的更陡下降 (recall 从 0.485 到 0.082) 为 SDGD 在大\n    schema 上的增益提供了动机。\n\n    '\n- name: DocRED Confusability Study\n  plan_id: exp-005\n  description: '在 DocRED (96 relation types) 上测试 confusability independence。 Document-level\n    RE 的 scaling stress test。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    count_1_f1: 0.095\n    count_1_recall: 0.21\n    count_6_f1: 0.082\n    count_12_f1: 0.075\n    count_24_f1: 0.068\n    count_48_f1: 0.058\n    count_96_f1: 0.042\n    pairwise_n_pairs: 4560\n    pairwise_pearson_r: 0.055\n    pairwise_pearson_p: 0.065\n    pairwise_nonzero_spearman_rho: 0.1\n    pairwise_nonzero_spearman_p: 0.12\n    per_type_partial_r: 0.08\n    per_type_partial_p: 0.32\n  result_rationale: 'DocRED 的 pairwise r 仅 0.055 (p=0.065，marginal)，原因：(1) document-level\n    RE 的核心难度在于 entity pair identification 和 multi-hop reasoning，这些 confound 远大于 type\n    confusability 的效应； (2) relation types 的 confusability 不仅来自语义相似 (如 headquarters_location\n    vs place_of_birth)， 还来自 entity type 重叠——两者难以通过 SCS 单一维度捕获；(3) 96 types 但 document-level\n    评估的 样本量和信号都比 sentence-level NER/ED 更稀疏。训练-free LLM RE 的整体 F1 极低 (0.04-0.10)， 在此性能区间，噪声掩盖了\n    confusability 信号。此结果建议：论文报告 DocRED 作为 \"scaling stress test\" 但承认 RE 任务的额外 confound\n    限制了 confusability 信号的可检测性。可在 appendix 报告， 不作为主 claim 的核心证据。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: DocRED Count Curve (Qwen3-32B, V2 prompt)\n    columns:\n    - count\n    - F1\n    - Precision\n    - Recall\n    rows:\n    - - 1\n      - 0.095\n      - 0.058\n      - 0.21\n    - - 6\n      - 0.082\n      - 0.055\n      - 0.175\n    - - 12\n      - 0.075\n      - 0.062\n      - 0.095\n    - - 24\n      - 0.068\n      - 0.07\n      - 0.066\n    - - 48\n      - 0.058\n      - 0.078\n      - 0.046\n    - - 96\n      - 0.042\n      - 0.085\n      - 0.028\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig (appendix): DocRED count curve。F1 极低 (0.04-0.10)，recall 下降趋势可见但 noisy。标注\n    training-free RE 的固有难度。'\n  analysis: 'DocRED 结果弱于预期，建议降级为 appendix 材料。主要价值：(1) 确认 count-recall 降解在 RE 任务上也存在\n    (Channel 1 task-agnostic)；(2) 暴露了 confusability 分析在 RE 上的局限—— type confusion 被更大的\n    task-specific confound 掩盖。论文不应将 DocRED 列为 Claim 1 的 核心证据，而是作为 \"boundary condition\"\n    讨论：confusability analysis 在 extraction 性能 极低 (<0.10 F1) 时信号被噪声淹没。如时间紧张 (P1 优先级)，可完全省略而不损害核心论点。\n\n    '\n- name: Interaction Effect 2x2\n  plan_id: exp-006\n  description: 'Few-NERD 上 {count_6, count_22} × {low_BCS, high_BCS} 的 2×2 factorial\n    design。 检验 count 和 confusability 的交互效应——additive vs multiplicative。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    count6_lowBCS_f1: 0.338\n    count6_highBCS_f1: 0.28\n    count22_lowBCS_f1: 0.318\n    count22_highBCS_f1: 0.245\n    count6_lowBCS_recall: 0.45\n    count6_highBCS_recall: 0.412\n    count22_lowBCS_recall: 0.295\n    count22_highBCS_recall: 0.248\n    count6_lowBCS_precision: 0.268\n    count6_highBCS_precision: 0.215\n    count22_lowBCS_precision: 0.352\n    count22_highBCS_precision: 0.243\n    count_main_effect_F: 8.2\n    count_main_effect_p: 0.006\n    count_main_effect_eta2: 0.12\n    bcs_main_effect_F: 5.1\n    bcs_main_effect_p: 0.028\n    bcs_main_effect_eta2: 0.08\n    interaction_F: 2.3\n    interaction_p: 0.135\n    interaction_eta2: 0.04\n    additive_prediction_HH: 0.25\n    actual_HH: 0.245\n    super_additive_residual: -0.005\n    count_effect_on_recall: -0.16\n    count_effect_on_precision: 0.052\n    bcs_effect_on_recall: -0.043\n    bcs_effect_on_precision: -0.081\n    n_per_cell: 12\n  result_rationale: 'Count 主效应显著 (F=8.2, p=0.006)：count_6 vs count_22 的 F1 差异 (~2.7\n    points) 主要由 recall 驱动 (0.431→0.272, Δ=-0.160)，确认 Channel 1 (count→recall) 机制。\n    BCS 主效应显著 (F=5.1, p=0.028)：low vs high BCS 的 F1 差异 (~6.5 points) 同时影响 recall 和\n    precision，但 precision 效应更大 (Δ=-0.081)，因为 type confusion 直接导致 precision 下降。 Interaction\n    不显著 (F=2.3, p=0.135)：additive 预测 (0.250) 与实际 (0.245) 仅差 0.5 point， slight super-additivity\n    因统计功效不足 (n=12/cell) 未达显著。机制解释：count 和 BCS 共享 下游 working memory 资源——当 count 已高时，BCS\n    的额外负担略微放大，但两个通道的主要机制 (attention allocation vs type discrimination) 仍大致独立。此结果支持\n    \"approximately orthogonal\" 但须将 \"orthogonal channels\" 措辞软化为 \"largely additive with\n    marginal interaction\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 2×2 Factorial Cell Means (F1 / Recall / Precision)\n    columns:\n    - ''\n    - Low BCS\n    - High BCS\n    - BCS Effect\n    rows:\n    - - Count=6\n      - 0.338 / 0.450 / 0.268\n      - 0.280 / 0.412 / 0.215\n      - -0.058 / -0.038 / -0.053\n    - - Count=22\n      - 0.318 / 0.295 / 0.352\n      - 0.245 / 0.248 / 0.243\n      - -0.073 / -0.047 / -0.109\n    - - Count Effect\n      - -0.020 / -0.155 / +0.084\n      - -0.035 / -0.164 / +0.028\n      - ''\n  - name: Two-Way ANOVA Results\n    columns:\n    - Source\n    - F\n    - p\n    - η²\n    - Verdict\n    rows:\n    - - Count (main)\n      - 8.2\n      - 0.006\n      - 0.12\n      - Significant\n    - - BCS (main)\n      - 5.1\n      - 0.028\n      - 0.08\n      - Significant\n    - - Count × BCS\n      - 2.3\n      - 0.135\n      - 0.04\n      - Not significant\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: 2×2 interaction plot。X 轴 count (6, 22)，Y 轴 F1，两条线 (low/high BCS)。近似平行但 high\n    count 端 BCS gap 略大 → mild super-additivity 可视化。附 error bars (±1 SE)。'\n  - 'Fig: Recall 和 Precision 分别的 2×2 interaction plot 并列。Recall 图中 count 线间距大 (Channel\n    1 dominant)，Precision 图中 BCS 线间距大 (Channel 2 dominant)。'\n  analysis: '两个 main effects 均显著 (p<0.05)，interaction 不显著 (p=0.135) → 支持 multi-channel\n    model 的 基本 additive 假设。但 η²(interaction)=0.04 虽不显著，方向是 super-additive (实际 HH 比预测\n    差 0.5 点)，须在论文中 transparent 报告。Channel decomposition 清晰：count 主要影响 recall (Δ=-0.160)，BCS\n    主要影响 precision (Δ=-0.081)。但 BCS 也影响 recall (Δ=-0.043)，说明 confusability 不仅导致 type\n    confusion (precision hit) 还导致部分 entity 被完全遗漏 (model 在 confusable types 间犹豫不决时选择不输出)。这为\n    Claim 2 提供细化： 两通道非完全正交，confusability 有 secondary recall 效应。\n\n    '\n- name: Error Taxonomy by BCS Bin\n  plan_id: exp-007\n  description: '系统 FP/FN 分类 (type_substitution / boundary_error / false_negative /\n    hallucination)， 按 BCS bin 分层。Claim 2 的 mechanistic evidence。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    high_bcs_type_substitution_pct: 0.47\n    high_bcs_boundary_error_pct: 0.12\n    high_bcs_false_negative_pct: 0.33\n    high_bcs_hallucination_pct: 0.08\n    low_bcs_type_substitution_pct: 0.18\n    low_bcs_boundary_error_pct: 0.15\n    low_bcs_false_negative_pct: 0.55\n    low_bcs_hallucination_pct: 0.12\n    mid_bcs_type_substitution_pct: 0.3\n    mid_bcs_false_negative_pct: 0.45\n    type_sub_monotonic_increase_with_bcs: true\n    false_neg_monotonic_decrease_with_bcs: true\n    boundary_err_monotonic: false\n    hallucination_monotonic: false\n    type_sub_ratio_high_vs_low: 2.6\n    chi2_type_sub_vs_bcs_bin: 18.4\n    chi2_p: 0.001\n  result_rationale: 'High-BCS batch 中 type_substitution 占 47%：当 batch 内包含语义相近的 types\n    (如 person-athlete vs person-artist)，模型正确识别 entity span 但选错 type——这正是 confusability\n    的直接机械效应。 Low-BCS batch 中 false_negative 占 55%：当 types 不 confusable 时，主要错误模式变为\n    entity 遗漏 (模型在 prompt 中看到多个不相关 types，attention 分散导致某些 types 的 entities 被忽略)。 趋势不完全干净的原因：(1)\n    boundary_error 不随 BCS 单调变化——它受 entity mention 的 surface form 模糊性影响 (如 \"New York\n    City\" vs \"New York\")，与 type confusability 部分独立； (2) hallucination 在各 bin 间波动 (8-12%)，因为\n    hallucination 主要由模型的 parametric knowledge 驱动，与 batch confusability 无关。Chi-square\n    检验确认 type_substitution 比例与 BCS bin 显著 相关 (p=0.001)，但整体 error taxonomy 不是完美的 four-way\n    separation。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Error Distribution by BCS Bin\n    columns:\n    - BCS Bin\n    - type_substitution\n    - boundary_error\n    - false_negative\n    - hallucination\n    - n_errors\n    rows:\n    - - '[0, 0.3)'\n      - 18%\n      - 15%\n      - 55%\n      - 12%\n      - 820\n    - - '[0.3, 0.5)'\n      - 30%\n      - 14%\n      - 45%\n      - 11%\n      - 540\n    - - '[0.5, 0.7)'\n      - 42%\n      - 11%\n      - 38%\n      - 9%\n      - 380\n    - - '[0.7, 1.0]'\n      - 52%\n      - 13%\n      - 28%\n      - 7%\n      - 260\n  - name: Monotonicity Summary\n    columns:\n    - Error Type\n    - Trend with BCS↑\n    - Monotonic?\n    - Chi² p\n    rows:\n    - - type_substitution\n      - ↑ (18→52%)\n      - 'Yes'\n      - '0.001'\n    - - boundary_error\n      - ≈flat (11-15%)\n      - 'No'\n      - '0.62'\n    - - false_negative\n      - ↓ (55→28%)\n      - 'Yes'\n      - '0.003'\n    - - hallucination\n      - ↓ slight (12→7%)\n      - No (non-monotonic at mid)\n      - '0.18'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Stacked bar chart，X 轴 BCS bin，Y 轴 error 比例。type_substitution (红) 随 BCS 增长明显，false_negative\n    (蓝) 随 BCS 下降。boundary_error 和 hallucination 相对稳定。'\n  - 'Fig: 典型错误案例展示 (qualitative)。High-BCS batch 中 person-athlete 被标为 person-artist\n    的实例；Low-BCS batch 中 entity 完全遗漏的实例。'\n  analysis: 'Error taxonomy 提供了 multi-channel model 最直接的 mechanistic 支持：type_substitution\n    从 18% (low BCS) 上升到 52% (high BCS)，false_negative 从 55% 下降到 28%。这确认了 confusability\n    驱动 type confusion (Channel 2) 而 count/attention dilution 驱动 entity omission (Channel\n    1)。 但趋势的不完全干净 (boundary_error 无 BCS 趋势、hallucination 非单调) 要求在论文中用 \"dominant error\n    modes shift\" 而非 \"exclusive channels\" 的措辞。Chi-square 显著 (p=0.001) 确保 type_substitution-BCS\n    关系有统计支撑。此分析与 exp-002 的 confusion ratio (10-28x) 互补——后者量化了 confusability 对混淆频率的影响，前者量化了\n    confusability 对 error 类型分布的影响。\n\n    '\n- name: Multi-Model Validation (LLaMA-3.3-70B)\n  plan_id: exp-012\n  description: '用 LLaMA-3.3-70B-Instruct 复现 exp-002 protocol on Few-NERD。 验证 confusability\n    independence 非 model-specific artifact。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    model2_full_schema_f1: 0.385\n    model2_full_schema_precision: 0.59\n    model2_full_schema_recall: 0.285\n    model2_count1_f1: 0.295\n    model2_count1_recall: 0.595\n    model2_count6_f1: 0.278\n    model2_count6_recall: 0.43\n    model2_count12_f1: 0.31\n    model2_count12_recall: 0.305\n    model2_count64_f1: 0.385\n    model2_count64_recall: 0.285\n    model2_pairwise_all_r: 0.09\n    model2_pairwise_all_p: 0.012\n    model2_pairwise_count6_r: 0.04\n    model2_pairwise_count6_p: 0.12\n    model2_pairwise_count12_r: 0.11\n    model2_pairwise_count12_p: 0.008\n    model2_pairwise_nonzero_spearman: 0.17\n    model2_pairwise_nonzero_p: 0.032\n    model2_f1_bcs_partial_r: 0.22\n    model2_f1_bcs_partial_p: 0.11\n    model2_f1_bcs_count12_r: 0.38\n    model2_f1_bcs_count12_p: 0.048\n    model2_per_type_partial_r: 0.15\n    model2_per_type_partial_p: 0.082\n    model2_confusion_ratio_extreme_count12: 7.5\n    model2_confusion_ratio_extreme_count6: 15.2\n    model2_top_pair: person-other <-> person-politician (BCS=0.934, confusion=118)\n  result_rationale: 'LLaMA-3.3-70B 的 pairwise r=0.09 弱于 Qwen3-32B 的 0.156，原因：(1) 不同模型家族对\n    type confusability 有不同的 sensitivity——LLaMA 的 instruction following 和 NER 能力与 Qwen\n    不同， 某些 confusable pairs (如 location subtypes) LLaMA 处理更好，其他 (如 person subtypes)\n    更差， 导致总体 BCS-confusion 相关被 partial cancellation 削弱；(2) LLaMA-3.3 在 70B scale 上的\n    in-context learning 能力可能使其对 type description 的 discrimination 更好，降低了 embedding\n    SCS 的预测力 (模型实际 confusion pattern 与 static embedding SCS 的偏差更大)。 count_6 pairwise\n    r 不显著 (p=0.12) 因为 6 types 下 confusion event 很少——每个 batch 只有 C(6,2)=15 个 type pair，大多数\n    confusion count 为 0，统计检验功效不足。count_12 仍显著 (r=0.11, p=0.008)。Top confused pair\n    仍是 person-other ↔ person-politician (确认 confusion 结构 model-agnostic)。整体全 schema\n    F1=0.385 略低于 Qwen3 的 0.414，可能因 70B < 32B (FP8 quantization 使 Qwen3-32B 的有效参数更多)\n    或 model architecture 差异。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Cross-Model Pairwise Comparison\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Qwen3-32B\n    - LLaMA-3.3-70B\n    - Direction Consistent?\n    rows:\n    - - Pairwise r (all)\n      - 0.156\n      - 0.09\n      - Yes (positive)\n    - - Pairwise p (all)\n      - '4.6e-12'\n      - 0.012\n      - Both significant\n    - - Pairwise r (count_6)\n      - 0.078\n      - 0.04\n      - Yes but LLaMA n.s.\n    - - Pairwise r (count_12)\n      - 0.147\n      - 0.11\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - Nonzero Spearman ρ\n      - 0.254\n      - 0.17\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - Confusion ratio (extreme, c12)\n      - 9.9x\n      - 7.5x\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - Top confused pair\n      - person-other↔politician\n      - person-other↔politician\n      - Same pair\n  - name: LLaMA-3.3-70B Count Curve\n    columns:\n    - count\n    - F1\n    - Precision\n    - Recall\n    rows:\n    - - 1\n      - 0.295\n      - 0.195\n      - 0.595\n    - - 6\n      - 0.278\n      - 0.208\n      - 0.43\n    - - 12\n      - 0.31\n      - 0.33\n      - 0.305\n    - - 22\n      - 0.275\n      - 0.315\n      - 0.245\n    - - 44\n      - 0.398\n      - 0.465\n      - 0.348\n    - - 64\n      - 0.385\n      - 0.59\n      - 0.285\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: 双模型 pairwise BCS-confusion scatter plot 并列。Qwen3 (左) 回归线 slope 更陡 (r=0.156)，LLaMA\n    (右) slope 更平 (r=0.09) 但方向一致。'\n  - 'Fig: 双模型 count curve 叠加在同一坐标系。两条 recall 线均单调下降，LLaMA 稍低但趋势平行。'\n  analysis: 'Multi-model validation 确认 confusability-confusion 关系非 model-specific：方向一致、top\n    confused pair 相同、confusion ratio 均为正。但效应量差异 (0.156 vs 0.09) 要求论文承认 \"effect size\n    varies across model families\"。count_6 在 LLaMA 上不显著是功效问题 (小样本 + 弱效应)， 不影响 main\n    claim。论文应报告 cross-model comparison table，强调方向一致性而非效应量匹配。 满足 reviewer \">=2 models\"\n    要求，但 reviewer 可能追问为什么效应量减半——准备好解释： 不同模型的 internal representation 与 static embedding\n    SCS 的对齐程度不同。\n\n    '\n- name: SDGD-zero on Few-NERD\n  plan_id: exp-008\n  description: 'Confusability-minimizing batch composition via embedding SCS + graph\n    coloring on Few-NERD (66 types)。 与 single-pass full-schema baseline 对比。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    scs_threshold: 0.5\n    n_edges_above_threshold: 85\n    chromatic_number: 10\n    avg_batch_size: 6.6\n    max_batch_size: 9\n    min_batch_size: 4\n    max_within_batch_scs: 0.42\n    sdgd_zero_f1: 0.437\n    sdgd_zero_precision: 0.405\n    sdgd_zero_recall: 0.474\n    single_pass_f1: 0.414\n    single_pass_precision: 0.648\n    single_pass_recall: 0.304\n    f1_gain_over_single: 2.3\n    n_merge_conflicts: 145\n    merge_conflict_resolution: confidence-based (max logprob)\n    pct_docs_with_conflicts: 0.18\n    sdgd_wrong_type_count: 1280\n    single_pass_wrong_type_count: 2050\n    wrong_type_reduction_pct: 0.375\n    api_calls_per_doc: 10\n    wall_clock_ratio_vs_single: 8.5\n  result_rationale: 'SDGD-zero 在 66-type Few-NERD 上增益有限 (+2.3 F1) 的原因：(1) 66 types\n    的 confusability 负担中等——只有 ~85 个 type pair SCS>0.5 (out of C(66,2)=2145)，graph coloring\n    的优化空间 有限；(2) single-pass baseline 在 V2 prompt 下已达 F1=0.414，under-prediction (pred/gold=0.47)\n    是主要瓶颈——SDGD 通过降低 batch size 提升了 recall (+0.170) 但同时降低了 precision (-0.243)， 因为小\n    batch 促使模型 over-predict；(3) merge step 引入 ~145 个 span conflict (18% docs 受影响)，\n    confidence-based resolution 不完美——部分 conflict 解决错误抵消了 confusability reduction 的收益。\n    Wrong type count 从 2050 降至 1280 (减少 37.5%) 是 SDGD 的直接 mechanistic 效果—— confusable\n    types 被分到不同 batch 后 type confusion 减少。但 F1 gain 仅 2.3 是因为 wrong type reduction\n    只是 overall error 的一部分——false negative 和 boundary error 未被 SDGD 直接解决。 结论：66 types\n    属于 \"中等 schema\"，SDGD 增益 marginal，consistent with median tier 定义。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: SDGD-zero vs Single-Pass on Few-NERD\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - Batches\n    - F1\n    - Precision\n    - Recall\n    - WrongType\n    - API Calls\n    rows:\n    - - Single-pass\n      - 1\n      - 0.414\n      - 0.648\n      - 0.304\n      - 2050\n      - 1\n    - - SDGD-zero\n      - 10\n      - 0.437\n      - 0.405\n      - 0.474\n      - 1280\n      - 10\n    - - Δ\n      - ''\n      - '+2.3'\n      - '-24.3'\n      - '+17.0'\n      - -37.5%\n      - '+9'\n  - name: SDGD Batch Composition Summary\n    columns:\n    - Batch\n    - Size\n    - Max Intra-Batch SCS\n    - Example Types\n    rows:\n    - - 1\n      - 7\n      - 0.38\n      - person-athlete, event-protest, product-car, ...\n    - - 2\n      - 6\n      - 0.35\n      - location-city, art-music, organization-company, ...\n    - - 3\n      - 8\n      - 0.42\n      - person-politician, building-library, event-election, ...\n    - - '...'\n      - '...'\n      - '...'\n      - '...'\n    - - 10\n      - 5\n      - 0.28\n      - other-disease, other-currency, other-language, ...\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: SDGD batch composition 可视化——confusability graph (nodes=types, edges=high\n    SCS pairs)，graph coloring 标注不同颜色。显示 person subtypes 被分到不同 batches。'\n  - 'Fig: Single-pass vs SDGD-zero bar chart (F1, P, R 三组 bars)。标注 F1 gain 和 recall\n    提升。'\n  analysis: 'Few-NERD 上 SDGD-zero 的 +2.3 F1 增益在统计上 marginal (需报 confidence interval)。\n    主要价值在于方向验证——wrong type reduction (37.5%) 确认 confusability-aware grouping 的 mechanistic\n    效果。但在 66-type schema 上，SDGD 的 practical significance 有限—— single-pass 已 decent，decomposition\n    的额外 API cost (10x) 可能不值得。 论文应将 Few-NERD 结果定位为 \"proof of concept\"，MAVEN 结果才是 \"practical\n    demonstration\"。 Precision-recall tradeoff (precision 下降 24 points but recall 上升\n    17 points) 需要在论文中 讨论：SDGD 的 batch size reduction 解决了 under-prediction 问题，但引入了\n    over-prediction。 future work 可结合 SDGD + per-type precision calibration。\n\n    '\n- name: SDGD-zero on MAVEN\n  plan_id: exp-009\n  description: 'SDGD-zero on MAVEN (168 event types)。与 single-pass + random batching\n    对比。 Cross-task validation of SDGD framework (NER→ED)。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    scs_threshold: 0.45\n    n_edges_above_threshold: 230\n    chromatic_number: 22\n    avg_batch_size: 7.6\n    max_batch_size: 11\n    min_batch_size: 5\n    max_within_batch_scs: 0.4\n    sdgd_zero_f1: 0.175\n    sdgd_zero_precision: 0.19\n    sdgd_zero_recall: 0.162\n    single_pass_f1: 0.135\n    single_pass_recall: 0.082\n    random_k22_f1: 0.155\n    random_k22_recall: 0.138\n    f1_gain_over_single: 4.0\n    f1_gain_over_random: 2.0\n    sdgd_vs_single_p: 0.002\n    sdgd_vs_random_p: 0.038\n    sdgd_wrong_type_count: 4200\n    single_pass_wrong_type_count: 11500\n    random_wrong_type_count: 6800\n    api_calls_per_doc: 22\n    wall_clock_ratio_vs_single: 18.5\n    wall_clock_ratio_vs_pertype: 0.2\n  result_rationale: 'MAVEN 上 SDGD-zero 增益更大 (+4.0 F1 over single-pass, +2.0 over random)\n    的原因： (1) 168 types 的 single-pass baseline 极差 (F1=0.135)——模型在一个 prompt 中处理 168\n    个 event type definition 时严重过载，recall 仅 0.082；SDGD 将 batch size 降至 ~7.6 types，\n    recall 从 0.082 提升至 0.162 (几乎翻倍)；(2) FrameNet 层级中 sibling types 的 BCS 很高 (119 pairs\n    > 0.5)，random batching 让这些 sibling 有 ~1/22 概率共现——SDGD 将此概率降至零， 减少了 FrameNet-specific\n    type confusion；(3) wrong type 从 11500 降至 4200 (63% reduction)， 远高于 Few-NERD 的\n    37.5%，说明 confusability-aware grouping 在大 schema 上价值递增。 SDGD vs random delta (+2.0\n    F1) 隔离了 confusability-aware grouping 的 contribution—— random 也帮助 (by reducing\n    count per batch) 但 SDGD 额外分离了 confusable types。 p=0.002 (vs single-pass) 和 p=0.038\n    (vs random) 确认显著性。 此结果是论文 Claim 3 的核心证据——在 ≥100 types 的大 schema 上 SDGD 有 practical\n    significance。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: SDGD-zero Comparison on MAVEN (168 types)\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - Batches\n    - F1\n    - Precision\n    - Recall\n    - WrongType\n    - p vs SDGD\n    rows:\n    - - Single-pass\n      - 1\n      - 0.135\n      - 0.34\n      - 0.082\n      - 11500\n      - 0.002\n    - - Random (k=22)\n      - 22\n      - 0.155\n      - 0.175\n      - 0.138\n      - 6800\n      - 0.038\n    - - SDGD-zero (k=22)\n      - 22\n      - 0.175\n      - 0.19\n      - 0.162\n      - 4200\n      - —\n  - name: Cross-Task SDGD Gain Summary\n    columns:\n    - Dataset\n    - Types\n    - SDGD-zero F1\n    - Single F1\n    - Δ F1\n    - Δ WrongType%\n    rows:\n    - - Few-NERD\n      - 66\n      - 0.437\n      - 0.414\n      - '+2.3'\n      - -37.5%\n    - - MAVEN\n      - 168\n      - 0.175\n      - 0.135\n      - '+4.0'\n      - -63.5%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: SDGD method comparison bar chart on MAVEN。三组 bars (single / random / SDGD-zero)，F1\n    + WrongType count 双 Y 轴。WrongType 的下降趋势与 F1 gain 呼应。'\n  - 'Fig: SDGD gain vs schema size scatter。X 轴 n_types (66, 168)，Y 轴 Δ F1。两个点 + 趋势线显示\n    gain 随 schema size 增长。附虚线标注 Claim 3 的适用范围 (≥100 types)。'\n  analysis: 'MAVEN 结果确认 SDGD 在大 schema (168 types) 上有 substantial 增益——F1 gain +4.0\n    显著 (p=0.002)。与 Few-NERD 的 +2.3 对比形成清晰趋势：SDGD 的价值随 schema complexity (type count\n    × confusability density) 递增。Cross-task 成功 (NER → ED) 支持 SDGD 的 task-agnostic 性质。Random\n    ablation (Δ=+2.0) 确认 confusability-aware grouping 的独立 贡献超越 mere batch count reduction。Wrong\n    type 63.5% 减少是 SDGD 的 headline mechanistic result。论文应将此作为 Claim 3 的 primary evidence，Few-NERD\n    作为 secondary。 局限性：absolute F1=0.175 仍很低——SDGD 改善了 relative performance 但 training-free\n    ED 在 168 types 上仍远落后 supervised method。须在论文中 frame 为 \"SDGD narrows the gap but\n    does not close it\" 并指出 remaining error 来自 non-confusability sources (count capacity,\n    event trigger ambiguity)。\n\n    '\n- name: SDGD-cal on Few-NERD\n  plan_id: exp-010\n  description: '用 5-10 calibration examples 构建 empirical confusion matrix，替换 embedding\n    SCS 做 graph coloring。对比 SDGD-zero。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_calibration_examples: 8\n    calibration_api_calls: 528\n    empirical_confusion_pairs_discovered: 42\n    overlap_with_scs_top50: 0.62\n    sdgd_cal_f1: 0.449\n    sdgd_cal_precision: 0.415\n    sdgd_cal_recall: 0.488\n    sdgd_zero_f1: 0.437\n    f1_gain_over_zero: 1.2\n    n_batches_changed: 4\n    types_reassigned: 8\n    new_chromatic_number: 11\n    sdgd_cal_vs_zero_p: 0.15\n  result_rationale: 'SDGD-cal 比 SDGD-zero 仅 +1.2 F1 的原因：(1) 8 个 calibration example\n    对 66×66 confusion matrix 的估计很稀疏——C(66,2)=2145 个 pair 中只有 ~42 个被经验观察到 confused，其余是零，\n    matrix 极度 sparse；(2) SCS top-50 confusable pairs 中 62% 与 empirical confusion 重合——\n    embedding proxy 已捕获主要 confusion 结构，calibration 只修正了 38% 的 \"surprise\" pairs； (3)\n    修正的 8 个 type 重新分配只影响了 4 个 batch，global batch structure 变化有限。 Calibration 的主要价值在于发现\n    SCS 低估的 confusable pairs (如 art-film ↔ art-broadcastprogram， SCS=0.38 但 empirical\n    confusion=12) 和 SCS 高估的 pairs (如 organization-religion ↔ organization-political，SCS=0.72\n    但 confusion=0)。p=0.15 不显著——在 66-type schema 上 calibration 的增量太小。此结果建议 SDGD-cal\n    的价值在大 schema 上更大 (where SCS noise affects more pairs)。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: SDGD-cal vs SDGD-zero on Few-NERD\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - F1\n    - P\n    - R\n    - Calibration Cost\n    rows:\n    - - SDGD-zero\n      - 0.437\n      - 0.405\n      - 0.474\n      - 0 examples\n    - - SDGD-cal\n      - 0.449\n      - 0.415\n      - 0.488\n      - 8 examples (528 API calls)\n    - - Δ\n      - '+1.2'\n      - '+1.0'\n      - '+1.4'\n      - ''\n  - name: SCS vs Empirical Confusion Discrepancies (Top 5)\n    columns:\n    - Type Pair\n    - SCS\n    - Empirical Confusion\n    - Direction\n    rows:\n    - - art-film ↔ art-broadcastprogram\n      - 0.38\n      - 12\n      - SCS underestimates\n    - - person-director ↔ person-actor\n      - 0.41\n      - 9\n      - SCS underestimates\n    - - organization-religion ↔ organization-political\n      - 0.72\n      - 0\n      - SCS overestimates\n    - - location-park ↔ location-island\n      - 0.65\n      - 1\n      - SCS overestimates\n    - - person-other ↔ person-scholar\n      - 0.88\n      - 45\n      - SCS accurate\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: SCS vs empirical confusion scatter。每个点是一个 type pair，X=SCS，Y=empirical confusion\n    count。标注 SCS 高估/低估的离群点。回归线 slope 可见但 scatter 大。'\n  analysis: 'Few-NERD 上 SDGD-cal 增益不显著 (p=0.15)，但 mechanistic insight 有价值：SCS 与 empirical\n    confusion 的 overlap 为 62% 意味着 embedding proxy 的 precision 约为 0.62——足以用于 zero-shot\n    SDGD 但有改进空间。SCS 的主要失败模式：(1) 低估跨 subtree 的 confusion (如 art-film ↔ art-broadcastprogram\n    在 Few-NERD hierarchy 中不是 direct sibling 但实际 highly confused)；(2) 高估有明确区分特征的 pairs\n    (如 religion ↔ political 虽语义相近但 entity mention 有明确 lexical 区分)。这些 insight 为 exp-015\n    (SCS validation) 提供预期框架。 对论文的贡献：SDGD-cal 作为 \"how much room for improvement exists\n    over zero-shot\" 的 upper bound indicator，即使在 66-type schema 上增量有限。\n\n    '\n- name: SDGD-cal on MAVEN\n  plan_id: exp-011\n  description: 'SDGD-cal on MAVEN (168 event types)。Empirical calibration on 168 types\n    with 5-10 examples。 Full comparison table。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_calibration_examples: 8\n    calibration_api_calls: 1344\n    empirical_confusion_pairs_discovered: 128\n    overlap_with_scs_top100: 0.48\n    sdgd_cal_f1: 0.192\n    sdgd_cal_precision: 0.205\n    sdgd_cal_recall: 0.18\n    sdgd_zero_f1: 0.175\n    f1_gain_over_zero: 1.7\n    sdgd_cal_vs_zero_p: 0.045\n    types_reassigned: 24\n    new_chromatic_number: 24\n    sdgd_cal_wrong_type: 3500\n    sdgd_zero_wrong_type: 4200\n    wrong_type_reduction_vs_zero: 0.167\n  result_rationale: 'SDGD-cal 在 MAVEN 上增益更大 (+1.7 F1, p=0.045 marginal significant)，原因：\n    (1) 168 types 使 SCS 的累积误差更大——SCS top-100 confusable pairs 中只有 48% 与 empirical\n    confusion 重合 (vs Few-NERD 的 62%)，因为 FrameNet 事件类型的细粒度语义区分在 embedding space 中表示不够准确\n    (如 Giving vs Commerce_sell, SCS=0.35 但 empirical confusion 高)； (2) calibration\n    发现了 24 个需要重新分配的 types (vs Few-NERD 的 8)，batch 结构变化更大； (3) wrong type 进一步减少 16.7%\n    (4200→3500) 确认 calibration 修正了 SCS 的 false negatives。 Marginal significance (p=0.045)\n    勉强过线，robustness 需额外 validation——如换 random seed 重复 calibration sampling，p 值可能波动到\n    0.05 以上。此结果支持 \"calibration 对大 schema 有价值\"，但收益的 cost-effectiveness (1344 额外 API\n    调用换 +1.7 F1) 需在论文中讨论。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Full Comparison Table — MAVEN\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - k\n    - F1\n    - P\n    - R\n    - WrongType\n    - Total API Calls\n    - p vs best\n    rows:\n    - - Single-pass\n      - 1\n      - 0.135\n      - 0.34\n      - 0.082\n      - 11500\n      - 710\n      - <0.001\n    - - Random (k=22)\n      - 22\n      - 0.155\n      - 0.175\n      - 0.138\n      - 6800\n      - 15620\n      - 0.005\n    - - SDGD-zero\n      - 22\n      - 0.175\n      - 0.19\n      - 0.162\n      - 4200\n      - 15620\n      - 0.045\n    - - SDGD-cal\n      - 24\n      - 0.192\n      - 0.205\n      - 0.18\n      - 3500\n      - 15620+1344\n      - —\n    - - Per-type\n      - 168\n      - 0.195\n      - 0.15\n      - 0.28\n      - 1800\n      - 119280\n      - 0.82\n  - name: Full Comparison Table — Few-NERD\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - k\n    - F1\n    - P\n    - R\n    - WrongType\n    - Total API Calls\n    - p vs best\n    rows:\n    - - Single-pass\n      - 1\n      - 0.414\n      - 0.648\n      - 0.304\n      - 2050\n      - 500\n      - 0.003\n    - - Random (k=10)\n      - 10\n      - 0.423\n      - 0.395\n      - 0.455\n      - 1650\n      - 5000\n      - 0.08\n    - - SDGD-zero\n      - 10\n      - 0.437\n      - 0.405\n      - 0.474\n      - 1280\n      - 5000\n      - 0.15\n    - - SDGD-cal\n      - 11\n      - 0.449\n      - 0.415\n      - 0.488\n      - 1100\n      - 5000+528\n      - —\n    - - Per-type\n      - 66\n      - 0.47\n      - 0.385\n      - 0.602\n      - 650\n      - 33000\n      - 0.18\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Full method comparison on MAVEN (grouped bar chart)。五种方法的 F1, P, R 三组 bars。标注\n    statistical significance brackets。'\n  - 'Fig: SDGD-cal vs SDGD-zero 的 batch reassignment 可视化 (MAVEN)。Sankey diagram 显示\n    calibration 后 24 个 types 从原 batch 迁移到新 batch。标注迁移原因 (SCS underestimate/overestimate)。'\n  - 'Fig: Cost-effectiveness plot。X=total API calls，Y=F1。五种方法标点，连 Pareto frontier。SDGD-zero\n    和 SDGD-cal 在 frontier 上，per-type 不在 (cost 太高 for marginal gain)。'\n  analysis: 'MAVEN 上 SDGD-cal 是最佳方法 (F1=0.192)，但与 per-type splitting (F1=0.195) 几乎持平\n    (p=0.82 no significant difference)——这出乎意料地好，因为 SDGD-cal 只用 24 batches vs per-type\n    的 168。Cost-effectiveness 是 SDGD 的核心卖点：相近质量，~15% latency。 Cross-dataset 对比揭示 SDGD\n    的适用范围：(1) ≥100 types: SDGD-zero already significant, SDGD-cal further improves;\n    (2) 30-66 types: gains marginal, calibration not cost-effective; (3) <30 types:\n    SDGD unnecessary (single-pass sufficient)。这为论文的 Claim 3 限定了清晰的 适用条件。Full comparison\n    table (两个 dataset × 五种方法) 是论文 Table 1 的核心。\n\n    '\n- name: Random Batching Ablation\n  plan_id: exp-013\n  description: 'Same batch count k as SDGD, random composition。隔离 confusability-aware\n    grouping 的增量贡献。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    random_k10_fewnerd_f1: 0.423\n    random_k10_fewnerd_precision: 0.395\n    random_k10_fewnerd_recall: 0.455\n    sdgd_zero_fewnerd_f1: 0.437\n    delta_fewnerd: 1.4\n    delta_fewnerd_p: 0.08\n    random_k22_maven_f1: 0.155\n    sdgd_zero_maven_f1: 0.175\n    delta_maven: 2.0\n    delta_maven_p: 0.018\n    random_mean_within_batch_bcs_fewnerd: 0.285\n    sdgd_mean_within_batch_bcs_fewnerd: 0.168\n    random_mean_within_batch_bcs_maven: 0.235\n    sdgd_mean_within_batch_bcs_maven: 0.145\n    random_f1_std_fewnerd: 0.008\n    random_f1_std_maven: 0.006\n    n_random_seeds: 5\n  result_rationale: 'Random batching vs single-pass 的增益 (Few-NERD +0.9, MAVEN +2.0)\n    来自纯粹的 batch size reduction (Channel 1 mitigation)——fewer types per batch → higher\n    recall。SDGD 的额外增益 (Few-NERD +1.4, MAVEN +2.0) 来自 confusability-aware grouping\n    (Channel 2 mitigation)—— within-batch BCS 从 random 的 0.285 降至 SDGD 的 0.168，减少了\n    type confusion。 Few-NERD 上 delta=1.4 仅 marginal significant (p=0.08) 因为 66 types\n    中 high-BCS pairs 少， random batching 已有 ~90% 概率将 confusable pairs 分开 (with 10 batches,\n    co-occurrence probability = 1/10 = 10%)。MAVEN 上 delta=2.0 significant (p=0.018)\n    因为 168 types 中 high-BCS pairs 更多 (119 pairs > 0.5)，random batching 只有 ~95.5% 概率分开\n    (with 22 batches, co-occurrence = 1/22 = 4.5%)——但 4.5% of 119 pairs ≈ 5.4 confusable\n    pairs 平均 仍同 batch，SDGD 将此降至零。Random F1 的跨 seed variance 很小 (σ=0.006-0.008)，确认\n    ablation 结果 robust。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Random vs SDGD Ablation\n    columns:\n    - Dataset\n    - Single-pass F1\n    - Random F1 (mean±σ)\n    - SDGD-zero F1\n    - Δ Random\n    - Δ SDGD-Random\n    - p (SDGD vs Rand)\n    rows:\n    - - Few-NERD (66)\n      - 0.414\n      - 0.423±0.008\n      - 0.437\n      - '+0.9'\n      - '+1.4'\n      - 0.08\n    - - MAVEN (168)\n      - 0.135\n      - 0.155±0.006\n      - 0.175\n      - '+2.0'\n      - '+2.0'\n      - 0.018\n  - name: Within-Batch BCS Analysis\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - Mean Within-Batch BCS (Few-NERD)\n    - Mean Within-Batch BCS (MAVEN)\n    rows:\n    - - Random\n      - 0.285\n      - 0.235\n    - - SDGD-zero\n      - 0.168\n      - 0.145\n    - - Reduction\n      - -41%\n      - -38%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Ablation bar chart。三组 bars (single / random / SDGD) on each dataset。标注 decomposition\n    (random - single = Channel 1 gain) and (SDGD - random = Channel 2 gain)。'\n  - 'Fig: 5 random seeds 的 F1 分布 (violin plot or dot plot) vs SDGD 的单点。可视化 SDGD consistently\n    above random。'\n  analysis: 'Ablation 成功隔离了两个 contribution：batch size reduction (Channel 1) 和 confusability-aware\n    grouping (Channel 2)。在 MAVEN 上两者贡献相当 (各 +2.0 F1)；在 Few-NERD 上 Channel 1 贡献较小 (+0.9)\n    因为 66 types 的 single-pass recall (0.304) 虽不高但不 catastrophic。 SDGD vs random delta\n    在 Few-NERD 上 marginal (p=0.08) 是可预期的——这正是 median tier 的 核心特征：SDGD 在中等 schema 上增益\n    marginal。论文应 frame 为：\"The confusability-aware contribution scales with schema\n    size: moderate on 66 types, significant on 168 types.\"\n\n    '\n- name: Per-Type Splitting Ablation\n  plan_id: exp-014\n  description: 'Per-type splitting (1 type per batch, UniNER-style)。质量上限 + latency\n    vs quality tradeoff。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    pertype_fewnerd_f1: 0.47\n    pertype_fewnerd_precision: 0.385\n    pertype_fewnerd_recall: 0.602\n    pertype_fewnerd_api_calls: 33000\n    pertype_fewnerd_wrong_type: 650\n    pertype_maven_f1: 0.195\n    pertype_maven_precision: 0.15\n    pertype_maven_recall: 0.28\n    pertype_maven_api_calls: 119280\n    pertype_maven_wrong_type: 1800\n    sdgd_vs_pertype_f1_ratio_fewnerd: 0.93\n    sdgd_vs_pertype_f1_ratio_maven: 0.897\n    sdgd_vs_pertype_latency_ratio_fewnerd: 0.18\n    sdgd_vs_pertype_latency_ratio_maven: 0.2\n    pertype_merge_conflicts_fewnerd: 850\n    pertype_pct_docs_with_conflicts_fewnerd: 0.72\n    pertype_merge_conflicts_maven: 2400\n    pertype_pct_docs_with_conflicts_maven: 0.85\n  result_rationale: 'Per-type splitting achieves highest recall (Few-NERD 0.602, MAVEN\n    0.280) because each entity type gets the model''s full attention — no competition\n    from other types. 但 precision 较低 (Few-NERD 0.385, MAVEN 0.150) 因为 count_1 的 over-prediction\n    问题 (pred/gold ~2.85-2.97)：当只给模型一个 type 时， 它倾向于将更多 spans 标为该 type。Merge step 产生大量\n    conflict (72-85% docs 受影响)——当同一 span 被多个 single-type passes 标注时，confidence-based\n    resolution 不完美。 SDGD/per-type F1 ratio 为 0.93 (Few-NERD) 和 0.90 (MAVEN)：SDGD 在\n    ~18-20% latency 下 达到 per-type 90-93% 的 F1——这是 cost-effective 的 \"sweet spot\"。Per-type\n    的 wrong type 更少 (650 vs SDGD 1280 on Few-NERD) 因为 type confusion 在单 type batch\n    中不可能发生——所有 wrong type 来自 merge conflict resolution 错误。MAVEN 上 per-type F1=0.195\n    与 SDGD-cal 的 0.192 几乎相同 (p=0.82)，但 API cost 是 7.5x (119280 vs 15620+1344)—— 这是\n    SDGD 最强的 practical argument。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Per-Type vs SDGD Tradeoff\n    columns:\n    - ''\n    - Few-NERD (66 types)\n    - MAVEN (168 types)\n    rows:\n    - - Per-type F1\n      - 0.47\n      - 0.195\n    - - SDGD-zero F1\n      - 0.437\n      - 0.175\n    - - SDGD-cal F1\n      - 0.449\n      - 0.192\n    - - SDGD-zero/Per-type F1\n      - 93.0%\n      - 89.7%\n    - - SDGD-cal/Per-type F1\n      - 95.5%\n      - 98.5%\n    - - SDGD Latency/Per-type Latency\n      - 18%\n      - 20%\n    - - Per-type Merge Conflicts\n      - 850 (72% docs)\n      - 2400 (85% docs)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Cost-effectiveness Pareto frontier。X=API calls (log scale)，Y=F1。标注 five\n    methods on both datasets。SDGD 在 Pareto frontier 上，per-type 在 frontier 外 (dominated\n    on MAVEN by SDGD-cal)。'\n  - 'Fig: Merge conflict analysis。Per-type 的 conflict 类型分布：correct resolution, type\n    error introduced by merge, span boundary error from merge。显示 merge 是 per-type\n    的主要 bottleneck。'\n  analysis: 'Per-type splitting 是 quality upper bound 但 cost prohibitive——在 MAVEN\n    上 119K API calls 换来的 F1 (0.195) 与 SDGD-cal 的 17K calls (0.192) 几乎相同。这个结果是论文最有力的\n    practical argument：\"SDGD achieves 93-99% of the decomposition upper bound at 18-20%\n    of the cost.\" Merge conflicts 是 per-type 的 Achilles heel——72-85% docs 有 conflict，resolution\n    引入新错误。 SDGD 的 batch 设计自然减少了 conflict (fewer batches = fewer merge opportunities\n    + each batch has non-confusable types so span overlap is less ambiguous)。论文应 frame\n    per-type as \"naive decomposition\" 的 upper bound，SDGD as \"principled decomposition\"\n    的 practical optimum。\n\n    '\n- name: SCS Validation (Embedding vs Empirical)\n  plan_id: exp-015\n  description: 'Spearman/Kendall rank correlation between embedding-based SCS and\n    empirical confusion matrix from calibration (exp-010)。验证 embedding proxy 的实际 utility。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    spearman_rho: 0.38\n    spearman_p: 1.0e-05\n    kendall_tau: 0.27\n    kendall_p: 3.0e-05\n    top50_pairs_precision: 0.62\n    top50_pairs_recall: 0.45\n    top100_pairs_precision: 0.48\n    top100_pairs_recall: 0.52\n    n_scs_overestimate: 35\n    n_scs_underestimate: 28\n    mean_scs_of_overestimates: 0.68\n    mean_scs_of_underestimates: 0.32\n    fewnerd_spearman: 0.42\n    maven_spearman: 0.34\n  result_rationale: 'Spearman ρ=0.38 的 moderate correlation 反映了 embedding SCS 作为 confusability\n    proxy 的 固有局限：(1) SCS 基于 type name/description 的 static embedding，而实际 confusion\n    受 entity mention surface form、context distribution、model-specific representation\n    共同影响—— static embedding 只能捕获其中的 semantic relatedness component；(2) 高 SCS 不必然导致\n    high confusion——有些语义相近的 types 有明确的 lexical/morphological cue 帮助区分 (如 organization-religion\n    vs organization-political，organizations named \"Church of X\" vs \"X Party\" 容易区分)；(3)\n    低 SCS pair 可能因 dataset-specific 原因 highly confused (如 art-film ↔ art-broadcastprogram，在\n    Few-NERD 中 film/TV 的 entity mention 经常相同)。 Few-NERD ρ=0.42 高于 MAVEN ρ=0.34 因为\n    NER 的 entity type 更直接反映在 entity mention 的 surface form 中 (proper nouns 有 type\n    signal)，而 event triggers 更 ambiguous (同一动词 可能是不同 event type)。Top-50 precision=0.62\n    意味着 SCS 推荐的 top-50 confusable pairs 中 62% 确实是 empirically confused——足以让 SDGD-zero\n    outperform random，但留有 calibration 改进空间。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: SCS Validation Summary\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Few-NERD\n    - MAVEN\n    - Overall\n    rows:\n    - - Spearman ρ\n      - 0.42\n      - 0.34\n      - 0.38\n    - - Kendall τ\n      - 0.3\n      - 0.24\n      - 0.27\n    - - Top-50 Precision\n      - 0.68\n      - 0.56\n      - 0.62\n    - - Top-50 Recall\n      - 0.5\n      - 0.4\n      - 0.45\n    - - n overestimates (SCS high, confusion low)\n      - 15\n      - 20\n      - 35\n    - - n underestimates (SCS low, confusion high)\n      - 10\n      - 18\n      - 28\n  - name: SCS Failure Mode Examples\n    columns:\n    - Type Pair\n    - SCS\n    - Empirical Confusion\n    - Failure Type\n    - Explanation\n    rows:\n    - - org-religion ↔ org-political\n      - 0.72\n      - 0\n      - Overestimate\n      - Distinctive entity lexical cues\n    - - location-park ↔ location-island\n      - 0.65\n      - 1\n      - Overestimate\n      - Rare co-occurrence in data\n    - - art-film ↔ art-broadcastprogram\n      - 0.38\n      - 12\n      - Underestimate\n      - Shared entity mentions (titles)\n    - - Giving ↔ Commerce_sell\n      - 0.35\n      - 8\n      - Underestimate\n      - Frame semantics not in embeddings\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: SCS vs empirical confusion scatter (log scale Y)。每点一个 type pair。回归线 + confidence\n    band。标注 overestimate zone (top-left) 和 underestimate zone (bottom-right)。Few-NERD\n    蓝点，MAVEN 红点。'\n  - 'Fig: Precision-recall curve for SCS as confusion predictor。X=recall，Y=precision，SCS\n    threshold 从高到低扫描。标注 optimal threshold point。'\n  analysis: SCS validation 为 SDGD 框架的 theoretical grounding 提供了关键证据：ρ=0.38 说明 embedding\n    SCS 是 \"useful but imperfect\" proxy。这解释了 (1) 为什么 SDGD-zero 优于 random (SCS 捕获了 主要\n    confusion 结构)，(2) 为什么 SDGD-cal 优于 SDGD-zero (calibration 修正了 SCS 的 38% false positive\n    + 55% false negative)，(3) 为什么 MAVEN 上 SCS 更不准确 (ρ=0.34 vs 0.42) 导致 SDGD-cal 在\n    MAVEN 上增益更大 (+1.7 vs +1.2)。 论文应将 SCS validation 放在 method section 作为 SDGD 的 justification：\n    \"We validate that embedding-based SCS provides a moderate but actionable signal\n    for type confusability (ρ=0.38), sufficient for zero-shot decomposition but improvable\n    with calibration.\" 此结果也回应 reviewer 对 \"confusability measure validity\" 的 concern——SCS\n    不完美但 empirically validated，且 imperfection 有清晰的 failure mode taxonomy。\n","numLines":1357,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1357}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Bdo4goEpRy57FdrWh33nFJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me now dispatch two reviewers in parallel according to the dream-review-full protocol:\n- R1: Methods + Experiments\n- R2: Novelty + Related Work\n\nThen I'll conduct the roundtable (Steps 1-4) and submit the final report.\n\nLet me launch both reviewers as parallel agents.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":45580,"cache_read_input_tokens":22929,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":45580},"output_tokens":23,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5eba5149-decb-42fd-9375-14d22c483592","uuid":"29a903f6-5858-49d0-aa92-b7f218e51ebc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Bdo4goEpRy57FdrWh33nFJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"论文已读完，实验设计参考已读取。现在按 full 模式 dispatch 两位 Reviewer 并行独立审稿。"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":45580,"cache_read_input_tokens":22929,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":45580},"output_tokens":23,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5eba5149-decb-42fd-9375-14d22c483592","uuid":"2641ab0f-605c-4c9d-aaa4-80abfb7ac734"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Bdo4goEpRy57FdrWh33nFJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0142VnT6oG5eTFgzjSEcL5VA","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a top ML venue paper review. Your focus area is **Methods and Experiments**. \n\nReview the paper below according to top ML venue standards (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept).\n\n## Paper Summary\nTitle: \"Multi-Channel Schema Degradation in Training-Free LLM Information Extraction: Isolating Confusability from Count\"\n\nThe paper studies why training-free LLM information extraction degrades on complex schemas. It proposes a multi-channel degradation model:\n- Channel 1: type count → recall decline (attention dilution)\n- Channel 2: type confusability → type substitution errors (disambiguation failure)\n\nThese are shown to be largely additive (interaction F=2.3, p=0.135). The paper operationalizes this into SDGD (Schema-DAG-Guided Decomposition) using graph coloring on a type similarity graph.\n\n## Key experimental details from the paper:\n\n**Datasets**: Few-NERD (66 NER types), MAVEN (168 event types), DocRED (96 relation types, supplementary)\n**Models**: Qwen3-32B (primary), LLaMA-3.3-70B-Instruct (cross-model validation)\n**Evaluation**: Span-level micro-F1, precision, recall; error taxonomy (type_substitution, boundary_error, false_negative, hallucination)\n\n### Claim 1 (Confusability independently predicts degradation):\n- Count curve: Recall drops monotonically with type count on both datasets\n- Pairwise BCS-confusion: Few-NERD r=0.156 (p=4.6e-12, n=1953); MAVEN r=0.09 (p=0.003, n=14028)\n- Extreme batch confusion ratio: 2.8-3.2x on MAVEN\n- Cross-model (LLaMA-70B): r=0.09, p=0.012, same top confused pair\n- Per-type partial r: MAVEN r=0.14 (p=0.11), LLaMA r=0.15 (p=0.082) — marginal\n\n### Claim 2 (Multi-channel model):\n- 2x2 factorial: {count=6, count=22} × {low BCS, high BCS} on Few-NERD\n- ANOVA: Count F=8.2 p=0.006 η²=0.12; BCS F=5.1 p=0.028 η²=0.08; Interaction F=2.3 p=0.135 η²=0.04\n- n=12 per cell\n- Error taxonomy: type_sub 18%→52% (low→high BCS), χ²=18.4 p=0.001\n\n### Claim 3 (SDGD effectiveness):\n- MAVEN: SDGD-zero +4.0 F1 over single-pass (p=0.002), +2.0 over random (p=0.038)\n- Few-NERD: SDGD-zero +2.3 F1 over single-pass (p=0.003)\n- SDGD-cal on MAVEN: F1=0.192, near per-type 0.195 (p=0.82) at 14% API cost\n- Random ablation: MAVEN SDGD vs random p=0.018; Few-NERD p=0.08\n- Per-type: quality upper bound but 72-85% docs have merge conflicts\n\n### SCS Validation:\n- Spearman ρ=0.38 (p<1e-5) overall; Few-NERD 0.42, MAVEN 0.34\n- Top-50 precision=0.62, recall=0.45\n\n### DocRED (boundary condition):\n- Pairwise r=0.055, p=0.065 (marginal)\n- Very low absolute F1 (0.04-0.10)\n\n## Experiment design reference (what was planned):\nThe full experiment plan included 11 experiments: MAVEN confusability study (exp-004), DocRED study (exp-005), 2x2 interaction (exp-006), error taxonomy (exp-007), multi-model validation with LLaMA (exp-012), SDGD-zero on Few-NERD (exp-008), SDGD-zero on MAVEN (exp-009), SDGD-cal on Few-NERD (exp-010), SDGD-cal on MAVEN (exp-011), random batching ablation (exp-013), per-type splitting ablation (exp-014), SCS validation (exp-015).\n\nThe paper appears to cover all planned experiments. DocRED is correctly positioned as supplementary/boundary condition.\n\n## Your review should cover:\n\n1. **Methodological soundness**: Is the experimental design rigorous? Are controls adequate? Are statistical tests appropriate?\n2. **Reproducibility**: Are enough details provided? Any missing information?\n3. **Statistical concerns**: Are the effect sizes meaningful? Are the p-values interpreted correctly? Any multiple comparison issues?\n4. **Experimental coverage**: Are the experiments sufficient to support the claims?\n5. **Specific weaknesses in methods/experiments**\n6. **Specific strengths in methods/experiments**\n\nProvide:\n- A structured review with sections for Summary, Strengths, Weaknesses, Questions for Authors, Minor Issues\n- A preliminary score (1-6) and confidence (1-5)\n- Be rigorous but fair. Note both what the paper does well and where it falls short.\n\nReport in under 1500 words."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":45580,"cache_read_input_tokens":22929,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":45580},"output_tokens":23,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5eba5149-decb-42fd-9375-14d22c483592","uuid":"12ecefcb-302c-4a32-8a5e-e1f857f96892"}
